the only crate allowed to talk to `tauri::*`."},"188":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#decision","content":"The axum router lives in `shalgalt-core::api` so `apps/desktop` and `apps/server`\nmount the same builder."},"189":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#consequences","content":"**Positive**"},"190":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#consequences","content":"`apps/server` ships without dragging Tauri into a server binary."},"191":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#consequences","content":"Future crates (e.g. `shalgalt-fileformat`, P4) follow a stable boundary pattern."},"192":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#consequences","content":"Shared `[profile.release]` lives at the workspace root — every crate inherits the\nsame LTO + strip settings."},"193":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#consequences","content":"**Negative**"},"194":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#consequences","content":"Compile times are slightly higher on the cold path (one extra link step per\ncrate); cached incremental builds are unaffected."},"195":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#consequences","content":"Path-based workspace deps require lockstep version bumps when we eventually\npublish (out of scope for v1.0)."},"196":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#follow-up","content":"ADR 0004 records the type-binding contract (ts-rs codegen) that follows naturally\nfrom the workspace shape."},"197":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0003-cargo-workspace-and-crate-boundaries#follow-up","content":"ADR 0005 records the IPC payload shape for the new `commands::pdf` module and how\nit stays inside the workspace's path-only Rule 1."},"198":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","type":"page","content":"ADR 0004 — TypeScript bindings via ts-rs","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen"},"199":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","content":"Generate the frontend's domain types from Rust with ts-rs and gate them in CI so the Rust/TS wire format never silently drifts."},"200":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#context","content":"Context"},"201":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"202":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#decision","content":"Decision"},"203":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"204":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"205":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#context","content":"`OmrTemplate` and the IPC payloads cross the Rust/TS boundary every time the editor\nsaves or loads a template, every time a scan emits progress, and every time results\nflow through axum. P0 maintained both halves by hand: a Rust struct with `serde`\nattributes and a parallel TypeScript interface. Two fields renamed in `template.rs`\nwithout updating `template.ts` would silently corrupt rows on read because the Zod\nschema would still accept the unknown shape."},"206":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Option"},"207":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Wire-format parity"},"208":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Toolchain weight"},"209":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"DX"},"210":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Hand-maintain TS interfaces (status quo)"},"211":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Manual, easy to drift"},"212":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Zero"},"213":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Poor — silent breakage"},"214":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Generate via OpenAPI / utoipa"},"215":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Schema-grade parity"},"216":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Heavy — needs HTTP doc"},"217":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Overkill for IPC"},"218":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"**`ts-rs` derives running inside `cargo test`**"},"219":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"**Wire-format parity**"},"220":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"**Light — one dep**"},"221":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"**Best — runs in workspace test pass**"},"222":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Generate via `specta` + `tauri-specta`"},"223":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Tight Tauri integration"},"224":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Couples codegen to Tauri"},"225":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#options-considered","content":"Loses `apps/server` reuse"},"226":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#decision","content":"CI runs `cargo test -p shalgalt-core --quiet` followed by\n`git diff --exit-code -- src/lib/types/generated`, so a Rust-side schema change that\nforgets re-generation fails the build."},"227":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#decision","content":"Conventions:"},"228":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#decision","content":"Hand-authored helpers (Zod schemas, `createEmptyTemplate`, `TemplateSummary`) live\nin `src/lib/types/template.ts` and re-export the generated types."},"229":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#decision","content":"`#[ts(optional)]` is reserved for `Option<T>` fields. For `Option`-equivalent\npatterns expressed via `serde(default, skip_serializing_if = …)` (e.g.\n`MarkerKind`), the Zod schema marks the field optional too — the `kind` field on\n`Marker` ships a `discriminatedUnion` schema with `.optional()` (P2-01 follow-up)."},"230":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#decision","content":"`i64` IDs widen to `#[ts(type = \"number\")]` because SQLite IDs always fit\n`Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` for our access patterns."},"231":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#consequences","content":"**Positive**"},"232":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#consequences","content":"Renames, additions, and field-type changes are caught by CI before they hit a\ntemplate-load corruption path."},"233":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#consequences","content":"`pnpm generate-types` (alias to `cargo test -p shalgalt-core --quiet`) gives the\nfrontend devs a one-command refresh."},"234":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#consequences","content":"**Negative**"},"235":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#consequences","content":"ts-rs prints a non-fatal warning for `#[serde(skip_serializing_if = …)]`. Cosmetic\nonly — emitted output is correct."},"236":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#consequences","content":"`export_to` paths resolve relative to one directory above the manifest dir, so\nworkspace-member crates use `../../../src/lib/types/generated/`. Documented inline\nin the derive macros."},"237":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#follow-up","content":"A future `prebuild` hook on `apps/web` could run the codegen automatically before\n`pnpm dev` starts; not pressing while the test-driven check covers CI."},"238":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0004-ts-rs-type-codegen#follow-up","content":"`MarkerKind` ergonomics: if the hand-authored Zod `.optional()` proves too easy to\nforget, we can move toward generated Zod (`zodios`-style) — out of scope for P2."},"239":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","type":"page","content":"ADR 0005 — PDF generation IPC contract","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract"},"240":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","content":"Path-string commands and on-disk results for the PDF render/preview IPC — never PDF bytes or data URLs across the Tauri bridge."},"241":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#context","content":"Context"},"242":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#decision","content":"Decision"},"243":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"244":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"245":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#context","content":"`shalgalt-pdf::render_template` returns a complete PDF byte stream. The editor needs\nto (a) write that stream to a user-picked path on disk, and (b) display a rasterized\npreview of it inside the editor pane without round-tripping the bytes through the\nwebview. Doing this naïvely tempts two anti-patterns:"},"246":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#context","content":"Sending the rendered PDF bytes through `invoke()` as a `Vec<u8>` or, worse, a\nbase64 string — millions of bytes per render, locking the IPC bridge for hundreds\nof milliseconds."},"247":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#context","content":"Embedding the PNG preview inside the same response payload as a data URL — same\ncost, plus inflates webview memory."},"248":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#context","content":"Master plan §6 fixes Rule 1 (\"paths only over IPC\") at the architecture level. This\nADR records exactly *how* the new PDF commands honor the rule."},"249":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#decision","content":"Conventions:"},"250":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#decision","content":"`template_json` is the serialized `OmrTemplate` (Rule 3 unit). Keeps the IPC\npayload uniform with how the frontend already serializes for the SQL plugin."},"251":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#decision","content":"`output_path` is the absolute path returned by the native save dialog\n(`pickPdfSavePath`). The save-dialog scope grants Tauri write permission for\nexactly that path even when it is outside the default `$APPDATA` capability."},"252":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#decision","content":"`pdf_render_template_preview` writes to `<APPCACHE>/preview/<sha256>.pdf`, then\nrasterizes the first page via the existing `shalgalt_cv::preview::rasterize_first_page`\nhelper. Returns the absolute PNG path, which the frontend feeds through\n`convertFileSrc(...)` to load via the `asset://localhost/` protocol."},"253":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#decision","content":"Both commands wrap the synchronous `printpdf` call in `tokio::task::spawn_blocking`\n(Rule 2), and both write to disk via `tokio::fs::write` so the async runtime stays\nfree for IPC traffic."},"254":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#decision","content":"Errors map to existing `AppError` variants (`BadRequest` for empty/invalid input,\n`Internal` for filesystem and render failures). New failure codes were considered\nbut rejected: the frontend toast surface already covers the user-facing shape, and\nadding error variants increases the API surface every consumer has to translate."},"255":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#decision","content":"Cache hygiene: `prune_old_previews` runs on app startup and drops `<APPCACHE>/preview/*`\nfiles older than 24 hours. Cleanup is best-effort; failure logs but never panics."},"256":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#consequences","content":"**Positive**"},"257":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#consequences","content":"IPC payloads stay below 100 KB even for the densest preset."},"258":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#consequences","content":"The rasterized preview reuses the asset-protocol helper introduced in P1, so we\navoid a second image-loading code path in the webview."},"259":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#consequences","content":"`pdf_generate_omr` is reused by P5's \"answer-key proof PDF\" feature without\nchanges — the variant flag is already accepted."},"260":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#consequences","content":"**Negative**"},"261":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#consequences","content":"The cache directory grows linearly until pruning runs at next app launch. For\npower users editing huge templates this can briefly hit dozens of MB. Acceptable\nfor a desktop app; not acceptable on mobile (out of scope)."},"262":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#consequences","content":"`template_json` parsing happens on every preview render. For very large templates\nthis is measurable (\\~1 ms on a midrange laptop for a 51-group preset); replacing\nit with a typed payload would require ts-rs-aware Tauri parameter binding, which\nis not currently supported by upstream."},"263":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#follow-up","content":"If the parsing cost ever shows up in profiling, switch the param to\n`template: OmrTemplate` once `tauri::command` learns to derive its parameter types\nfrom `ts-rs`-derived structs."},"264":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0005-pdf-ipc-contract#follow-up","content":"Multi-variant batch export (P5) reuses this command — the `variant` parameter is\nalready plumbed through to `PdfOptions::variant`."},"265":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","type":"page","content":"ADR 0006 — Light theme & comfort typography","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography"},"266":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","content":"Make light the default theme via mode-watcher with dark opt-in, and add a one-toggle comfortable type scale driven by CSS variables."},"267":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#context","content":"Context"},"268":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Options considered for theme"},"269":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"Options considered for comfort sizing"},"270":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"Decision"},"271":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"272":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"273":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#context","content":"The primary persona (master plan §1) is a Mongolian K–12 teacher who is **not** a\nsoftware professional. Two empirical constraints shaped the visual direction:"},"274":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#context","content":"Classroom monitors and projectors are usually mid-grade IPS or VA panels with\nwashed-out blacks, so a dark IDE chrome reads as low-contrast murk."},"275":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#context","content":"Older teachers — the median age of our beta cohort is \\~52 — read 16 px UI text\nat a noticeably slower rate than 18 px text on the same hardware."},"276":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#context","content":"P0 shipped the app dark-only. We need light as the default, dark as opt-in, **no**\nhigh-contrast mode (would force a third palette pair), and a one-toggle comfort\nmode that bumps the entire scale a notch without per-component CSS."},"277":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Option"},"278":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Implementation cost"},"279":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Persistence"},"280":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Per-screen drift risk"},"281":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Hand-rolled theme controller (`window.matchMedia` + manual class flip)"},"282":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Medium"},"283":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Need to hand-roll `localStorage` glue"},"284":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"High"},"285":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"**`mode-watcher` (already a dev dep)**"},"286":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"**Low**"},"287":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"**Built-in**"},"288":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"**Low**"},"289":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"CSS `@media (prefers-color-scheme)` only"},"290":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"Lowest"},"291":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"None — user can't override"},"292":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-theme","content":"High"},"293":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"Option"},"294":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"Pe