dered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"**`data-comfort` attribute on `<html>` + CSS variables on `:root[data-comfort=…]`**"},"302":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"**None — body font-size cascades**"},"303":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"**Instant**"},"304":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"**Acceptable**"},"305":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"Toggle a stylesheet at runtime"},"306":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"Medium"},"307":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"Flicker on swap"},"308":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#options-considered-for-comfort-sizing","content":"Acceptable"},"309":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"**Theme (P2-09)**"},"310":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"Mount `<ModeWatcher defaultMode=\"light\" />` in `src/routes/+layout.svelte`."},"311":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"Move the dark palette under `.dark`; everything in `:root` now defines the light\npalette. Both legacy `--color-*` and the shadcn surface (`--background`, `--card`,\n`--primary`, plus new `--success` and `--warning`) gain light + dark values."},"312":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"`ThemeToggle.svelte` exposes light / dark / system via `setMode(...)` from\n`mode-watcher`. Mounted in the sidebar footer."},"313":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-47","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"Color tokens use OKLCH so contrast ratios stay predictable across hue rotations.\nBody text on background: AA (4.5:1+) in both modes; primary button on\n`--primary-foreground`: AAA (7:1+) in both modes."},"314":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-48","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"**Comfort typography (P2-10)**"},"315":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-49","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"Define `--text-{xs,sm,base,lg,xl,2xl}`, `--button-h`, `--hit-min` on `:root`\n(default scale: 12 / 14 / 16 / 18 / 22 / 28 px; 40 px button height)."},"316":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-50","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"`:root[data-comfort=\"comfortable\"]` overrides every token one notch up\n(14 / 16 / 18 / 20 / 24 / 32 px; 48 px button height)."},"317":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-51","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"Body inherits `font-size: var(--text-base)`, so the toggle reflows the entire\napp instantly without per-component edits."},"318":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-52","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"`comfortMode` runes-store mirrors the choice to `<html data-comfort=…>` and\npersists to `localStorage` under `shalgalt-omr.comfort-mode`."},"319":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-53","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"`ComfortToggle.svelte` lives next to `ThemeToggle.svelte` in the sidebar footer."},"320":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-54","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#decision","content":"`Button` component default size is **not** updated to `min-h-[var(--button-h)]`\nin this iteration. Every existing button currently relies on shadcn's\n`h-7 / h-8 / h-9` ladder; a global flip would shift dialogs and toolbars across\nthe app at once. The `--button-h` token is in place so we can do the swap as a\none-line edit when we have layout coverage."},"321":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-55","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#consequences","content":"**Positive**"},"322":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-56","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#consequences","content":"Light is the default for fresh installs; existing dev installs persist their\nprior choice through `mode-watcher`'s storage."},"323":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-57","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#consequences","content":"Comfort mode is two clicks of CSS away from being applied to any new component\nvia `text-base` / `min-h-[var(--button-h)]` utilities."},"324":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-58","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#consequences","content":"`--success` and `--warning` tokens make it easier to retire ad-hoc green/yellow\nTailwind utilities in P3 (grading) and P4 (file format)."},"325":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-59","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#consequences","content":"**Negative**"},"326":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-60","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#consequences","content":"Existing buttons stay on the shadcn `h-8` ladder until the follow-up."},"327":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-61","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#consequences","content":"Comfort mode does not currently scale icons inside buttons — they use the\nshadcn `size-4` Tailwind utility. Pragmatic tradeoff; reads fine in user\ntesting because the body line-height grows around them."},"328":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-62","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#follow-up","content":"Promote the `Button` default size to `min-h-[var(--button-h)]` once the editor\ntoolbar layout is QA'd at 48 px."},"329":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography-63","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0006-light-theme-and-comfort-typography#follow-up","content":"If comfort mode ever needs an \"extra-comfortable\" notch (20 → 24 px body),\nadd `:root[data-comfort=\"extra-comfortable\"]` instead of overloading the\ncurrent attribute value."},"330":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"page","content":"ADR 0007 — Canvas wrapper & layout modules","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules"},"331":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","content":"A Canvas drawing-surface wrapper plus a module-per-visual-element layout split for shalgalt-pdf."},"332":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"Context"},"333":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"334":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"Wrapper layer"},"335":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"Module layout"},"336":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#decision","content":"Decision"},"337":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#b--canvas-wrapper","content":"B — `Canvas` wrapper"},"338":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"D — Module-per-element layout"},"339":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"340":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#positive","content":"Positive"},"341":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#negative","content":"Negative"},"342":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"343":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"P2-06 shipped a renderer where every layout module reached straight into `printpdf`'s\nlow-level `Op` enum. Within one P2-06 follow-up session four bug categories surfaced and\neach had to be diagnosed in a *different* file:"},"344":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"**Cursor accumulation in BT/ET.** `Op::SetTextCursor` compiles to PDF `Td` (relative\nmove). Two cursors inside one text section *add*. Bubble labels stacked on the first\nbubble of every group — diagnosed in `bubble_grid.rs`."},"345":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"**Sidebar font fallback.** Mongolian Cyrillic instructions rendered as `.notdef`\nboxes when the caller passed `NotoSansMongolian` to a sidebar that should have used\nLatin/Cyrillic Noto Sans — diagnosed in `sidebar.rs` + `lib.rs`."},"346":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"**Inside-circle digit position.** Centring math (offset by 30 % of glyph height)\nwas duplicated wherever an in-bubble label was drawn — diagnosed in `bubble_grid.rs`."},"347":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"**Row-label alignment.** Right-aligning a label against a bubble required hand-rolled\nwidth estimation at every call site — diagnosed in `labels.rs`."},"348":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"Each of the four bugs was a one-line fix, but they all shared a symptom: low-level PDF\noperators were being emitted from too many places, and the surrounding state (active\ntext section, current font, current text matrix) was implicit."},"349":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"A market survey of mainstream OMR tools (AMC, Remark Office, OMRChecker, OpenMCR,\nZipGrade) confirmed that **none** drives `printpdf`-equivalent low-level ops directly:\nAMC sits on `pdfTeX`, Remark on Word, the others ship pre-baked PDFs. The closest\nprior art for our pure-Rust path is AMC's `automultiplechoice.sty` LaTeX wrapper, which\nis *itself* a thin DSL over a lower-level engine."},"350":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"Two coupled decisions land here so the next phase (P3 CV pipeline) does not have to\nre-litigate them:"},"351":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"**Should layout modules emit raw `Op`s or go through a wrapper?**"},"352":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#context","content":"**How should the layout submodules be organised?**"},"353":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"Option"},"354":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"Where the BT/ET / cursor / colour state lives"},"355":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"Cost to migrate"},"356":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"A. Status quo (raw `Vec<Op>`)"},"357":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"scattered across `bubble_grid` / `labels` / `header` / `sidebar` / `manual_entry`"},"358":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"None"},"359":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"**B. `Canvas` thin wrapper**"},"360":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"one module owns BT/ET reset, font handle, colour, line width"},"361":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"\\~150 LOC migration, +5 unit tests"},"362":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"C. `genpdf`-style layout engine"},"363":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"hidden — but layout decisions move into the engine"},"364":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#wrapper-layer","content":"Rewrite, breaks Rule 3 contract"},"365":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"Option"},"366":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"Module count"},"367":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"Coupling"},"368":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"**D. One submodule per visual element** (markers, header, bubble\\_grid, labels, manual\\_entry, numeric\\_block, section\\_headers, sidebar)"},"369":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"8"},"370":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"Each module imports `Canvas` + `coords` only"},"371":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"E. One mega-module `layout.rs`"},"372":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"1"},"373":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"Tight"},"374":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"F. Per-section modules (cipher, variant, section1, section2)"},"375":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"4"},"376":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#module-layout","content":"Each duplicates label / underline code"},"377":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#b--canvas-wrapper","content":"`crates/shalgalt-pdf/src/canvas.rs` is the only module that emits text-related\n`Op`s. Everything else calls intent-shaped helpers:"},"378":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-47","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#b--canvas-wrapper","content":"Every `Canvas::text*` call wraps its own `StartTextSection` / `EndTextSection`. The\ntext matrix never accumulates across calls — bug #1 is mechanically impossible going\nforward. Bug #3's centring math lives in one method. Bugs #2 and #4 reduce to \"pass\nthe right `FontId`\" / \"use `text_right_aligned`\" — both visible at the call site."},"379":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-48","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#b--canvas-wrapper","content":"`Op` is still re-exported (`canvas::push`) as an escape hatch for primitives the\nwrapper does not yet cover (graphics-state save/restore, text-matrix rotation in\n`sidebar.rs`)."},"380":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-49","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"`markers.rs` — 4 corner alignment squares"},"381":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-50","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"`header.rs` — 2-column page header (title left + school right)"},"382":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-51","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"`bubble_grid.rs` — circles only — labels owned by `labels.rs`"},"383":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-52","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"`labels.rs` — row labels (right-aligned)"},"384":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-53","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"`manual_entry.rs` — cipher handwriting underlines"},"385":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-54","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"`numeric_block.rs` — delegates to `bubble_grid`"},"386":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-55","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"`section_headers.rs` — 1-Р ХЭСЭГ / 2.x stickers"},"387":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-56","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"`sidebar.rs` — top-right horizontal САНАМЖ block"},"388":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-57","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#d--module-per-element-layout","content":"Each module is ≤ 100 LOC. The split matches the spec sections in\n`docs/MONGOLIAN_OMR_SPEC.md` one-to-one — when the spec\ngains a new visual element, exactly one new submodule lands."},"389":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-58","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#positive","content":"The four cursor / font / centring / alignment bugs are now mechanically prevented\nrather than caught by code review."},"390":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-59","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#positive","content":"Layout modules read top-down as \"draw circle, draw label, draw header\" — the PDF\nvocabulary is gone."},"391":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-60","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#positive","content":"Adding a new visual element is one small file plus one register line in\n`layout/mod.rs`."},"392":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-61","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#positive","content":"Tests for layout primitives live in `canvas.rs` (5 unit tests pin BT/ET pairing,\nwidth estimation, in-circle centring)."},"393":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-62","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#negative","content":"One extra module + about 200 LOC of wrapper code."},"394":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-63","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#negative","content":"`printpdf` API changes are now centralised at the `Canvas` boundary — easier to\nupdate, but every renderer module reads against the wrapper, not the upstream."},"395":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-64","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#negative","content":"The Mongolian-script `sidebar.rs` still needs `Op` directly for the rotation-matrix\ncase (kept as `canvas.push(Op::SetTextMatrix { … })`) — pure-wrapper migration is\ndeferred until traditional Mongolian script support actually lands."},"396":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-65","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#follow-up","content":"ADR 0008 documents the in-circle bubble-label decision that the Canvas wrapper\nenabled."},"397":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-66","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#follow-up","content":"Layout-spec changes follow the procedure in\n`docs/MONGOLIAN_OMR_SPEC.md` §7 — issue + spec doc + TS\npreset + Rust fixture + golden regen, all in the same PR."},"398":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules-67","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0007-canvas-wrapper-and-layout-modules#follow-up","content":"A future LayoutMap sidecar (AMC's `.xy` pattern, master-plan D4) will plug into the\nCanvas at the call site without changing the wrapper API."},"399":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"page","content":"ADR 0008 — Bubble label position","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position"},"400":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","content":"Option labels are printed inside the bubble circle, matching the Mongolian-school OMR idiom and AMC prior art."},"401":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#context","content":"Context"},"402":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"403":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#decision","content":"Decision"},"404":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#why-this-works-for-cv","content":"Why this works for CV"},"405":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#section-header-semantics","content":"Section-header semantics"},"406":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"407":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#positive","content":"Positive"},"408":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#negative","content":"Negative"},"409":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"410":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#context","content":"P2-06 acceptance criterion #17 specified &#x2A;\"each circle carries a 1-character label drawn\n**next to** it\"*. The renderer faithfully implemented this and produced a card with\n≈ 520 floating glyphs scattered around the bubble grid — 30 × 4 next to every Section-1\nrow plus ≈ 200 next to Шифр/Section-2 digit bubbles. The output was not usable as an\nOMR card."},"411":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#context","content":"The acceptance criterion was wrong. The follow-up question — *where* should the label\ncharacter live? — has only a few credible answers and a real OMR-design tradition to\ndraw on."},"412":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Option"},"413":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Where the `'A'` glyph appears"},"414":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Real-world precedent"},"415":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"CV impact"},"416":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"A. Next to every bubble (P2-06 original)"},"417":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"tucked beside each circle"},"418":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Almost nobody"},"419":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Visual noise; CV unaffected"},"420":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"**B. Inside the circle**"},"421":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"centred inside the bubble outline"},"422":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"**AMC** (`\\AMCchoiceLabel`), most Mongolian-school cards"},"423":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"None — fully inked answer covers the printed glyph"},"424":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"C. Column header strip per section"},"425":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"one row of `A B C D E` above each block"},"426":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"OMRChecker, OpenMCR, Indian-style sheets"},"427":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Adds a section-anchored marker; CV must skip the strip"},"428":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"D. No label, key only"},"429":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"nothing on the printed sheet"},"430":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Stylised, modern templates"},"431":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"Student must memorise meaning"},"432":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#options-considered","content":"The market survey documented in `memory/project_omr_market_research.md`\nshows AMC (FOSS reference implementation) lands on B. Mongolian general-school cards\nmatch — see the reference photo at the time of issue #75. OMRChecker and OpenMCR\nland on C, but their inputs are *bitmap* OMR sheets where the column header is also a\nvisual marker for the threshold pass; we generate the sheets ourselves and have ArUco\nmarkers (P3-01) for that role."},"433":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#decision","content":"implemented in `crates/shalgalt-pdf/src/canvas.rs` (see ADR 0007).\nAuto-fits the font to ≈ 65 % of the bubble diameter (≈ 6 pt for the 3 mm bubble locked\nin `docs/MONGOLIAN_OMR_SPEC.md` §4), within the OMR-spec\ntarget range of 6–8 pt for in-bubble identifiers."},"434":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#why-this-works-for-cv","content":"The CV pipeline (P3-01 / P3-02) thresholds the *fraction of dark pixels inside a\nbubble*. The printed label is a thin glyph hull; a fully-inked answer fills the whole\ncircle and dwarfs the glyph's contribution. With:"},"435":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#why-this-works-for-cv","content":"3 mm bubble area = π × 1.5² = 7.07 mm²"},"436":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#why-this-works-for-cv","content":"6 pt glyph hull (rough): ≈ 1.0 mm²"},"437":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#why-this-works-for-cv","content":"Threshold for \"filled\" (per master plan §6.5): bubble fraction ≥ 0.35"},"438":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#why-this-works-for-cv","content":"the printed label contributes ≈ 14 % fill, well below the 0.35 threshold. The\n`crates/shalgalt-pdf/tests/labels_layout.rs` regression test\npins the upper bound on text-op count so the renderer cannot silently regress to\nOption A and double-count labels."},"439":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#section-header-semantics","content":"Sub-block stickers (`2.1`, `2.2`, `2.3`, `2.4`) and parent labels (`1-Р ХЭСЭГ`,\n`2-Р ХЭСЭГ`) are emitted by `crates/shalgalt-pdf/src/layout/section_headers.rs`\nand are NOT a column-header strip — they label the *block*, not each column position.\nШифр / Вариант suppress their headers (the geometry is self-evident)."},"440":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#positive","content":"The card matches the visual idiom of every real Mongolian-school OMR sheet shipped\nto date."},"441":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#positive","content":"AMC interop (future LayoutMap sidecar — see master plan D4) becomes a coordinate\ntranslation problem only; the visual semantics already match."},"442":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#positive","content":"One glyph per bubble, period — no per-bubble label X/Y math at any call site."},"443":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#negative","content":"3 mm bubbles + 6 pt in-bubble glyphs are at the small end of legibility. P5 may add a\n\"comfortable\" mode (4 mm bubble + 8 pt glyph) for low-vision printing, gated behind a\nuser setting."},"444":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#negative","content":"The CV pipeline must not be tuned to look *for* the glyph (e.g., template-matching\nthe printed `A`); it should treat the bubble as a uniform threshold target."},"445":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#follow-up","content":"The legibility / fill-fraction trade-off is parameterised in\n`crates/shalgalt-pdf/src/canvas.rs` — the\n`0.65` ratio in `text_centered_in_circle` is the lever to revise if classroom\ntesting reports glyphs are bleeding into the answer mark."},"446":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0008-bubble-label-position#follow-up","content":"ADR 0007 covers the wrapper that this decision relies on."},"447":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","type":"page","content":"ADR 0009 — ArUco corner markers","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers"},"448":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","content":"DICT_6X6_50 markers with IDs 0–3 in TL/TR/BR/BL order replace anonymous corner squares."},"449":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#context","content":"Context"},"450":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"451":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#decision","content":"Decision"},"452":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"453":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"454":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#context","content":"P0/P1 templates carried four solid corner squares as the visual reference points the\nCV pipeline relies on for perspective alignment. Solid squares are simple to print and\neasy to find with a contour-based detector, but they have two drawbacks:"},"455":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#context","content":"**No identity.** Four indistinguishable squares cannot tell the CV pipeline which\none is \"top-left.\" If a teacher feeds a sheet upside down or sideways into a\nscanner, the pipeline either guesses the orientation (brittle) or refuses the\npage (annoying for the teacher)."},"456":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#context","content":"**No error detection.** A scribble in a corner of the page can easily be mistaken\nfor the marker. We get no help from the marker geometry."},"457":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#context","content":"ArUco markers solve both problems at the cost of slightly larger printed glyphs.\nEach marker is a self-identifying 2D barcode with a single integer ID and a\nfixed bit pattern. The ArUco detector returns a `(corners, id)` pair per match, so\nslot resolution is built into detection."},"458":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"Option"},"459":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"Identity"},"460":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"Error detection"},"461":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"Marker size on A4"},"462":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"Detector availability"},"463":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"Solid corner squares (P0/P1)"},"464":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"none"},"465":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"none"},"466":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"\\~6 × 6 mm"},"467":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"bespoke contour detector"},"468":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"QR code (full L1)"},"469":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"high"},"470":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"high"},"471":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"\\~25 × 25 mm"},"472":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"OpenCV `QRCodeDetector`"},"473":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"ArUco DICT\\_4X4\\_50"},"474":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"per-marker"},"475":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"minimal — only 16-bit data"},"476":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"\\~6 × 6 mm (small)"},"477":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"OpenCV `aruco::detectMarkers`"},"478":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"**ArUco DICT\\_6X6\\_50**"},"479":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"per-marker"},"480":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"one-bit Hamming distance ≥ 4 between dictionary entries"},"481":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"\\~8 × 8 mm"},"482":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"OpenCV `aruco::detectMarkers`"},"483":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"ArUco DICT\\_7X7\\_1000"},"484":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"per-marker"},"485":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"strong"},"486":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"\\~10 × 10 mm"},"487":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#options-considered","content":"OpenCV `aruco::detectMarkers`"},"488":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#decision","content":"Rationale:"},"489":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#decision","content":"**DICT\\_6X6\\_50** is a sweet spot. The 6×6 inner data grid plus the mandatory\n1-cell black border gives an 8×8 cell footprint. At 200 DPI on A4 portrait this\nprints at roughly 8 × 8 mm — small enough to fit comfortably inside the 12 mm\nouter margin we already reserve for markers, large enough that a 200 DPI raster\nretains 4-5 pixels per cell which is well within `ArucoDetector`'s tolerance."},"490":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#decision","content":"**IDs 0..3** are the smallest non-overlapping identifier set the dictionary\nexposes. Using consecutive IDs makes the slot-to-position mapping trivial:\n`markers[i]` carries ID `i`, and `i ∈ {0, 1, 2, 3}` maps directly to TL/TR/BR/BL."},"491":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#decision","content":"**TL/TR/BR/BL** ordering matches the existing `OmrTemplate.markers: [Marker; 4]`\nconvention from `crates/shalgalt-core/src/domain/template.rs`. The grading\nengine, the printpdf renderer, and the perspective-warp routine all consume the\narray in this order."},"492":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#consequences","content":"The Mongolian-standard preset migrates from `MarkerKind::Square` to\n`MarkerKind::Aruco6x6 { ids: [0, 1, 2, 3] }`. The four-element `ids` field is\ncarried verbatim per marker — at PDF render time, slot index `i` indexes the\n`ids` array to pick which canonical bit pattern to paint."},"493":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#consequences","content":"`crates/shalgalt-pdf/src/layout/markers.rs` ships hardcoded canonical\n`DICT_6X6_50` bit patterns for IDs 0..3 only. Other IDs are not currently\nneeded; if a future template requires them, the table must be regenerated from\nOpenCV's predefined dictionary using the helper described in the module-level\ncomment."},"494":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#consequences","content":"`crates/shalgalt-cv/src/perspective.rs` carries both ArUco bindings behind\ncfg gates: legacy `cv::aruco::detectMarkers` for OpenCV 4.6 (Ubuntu / Debian\napt, older Homebrew bottles) and modern `cv::objdetect::ArucoDetector` for\nOpenCV 4.7+ (Windows self-extractor, current Homebrew, vcpkg).\n`crates/shalgalt-cv/build.rs` probes the local OpenCV version and emits one\nof `opencv_aruco_legacy` / `opencv_aruco_modern`. `OPENCV_FORCE_ARUCO=legacy\n|modern` overrides the probe for environments where it cannot read the\nversion (e.g. Windows without pkg-config, vcpkg manifest mode). Both APIs\naccept `DICT_6X6_50`; the assemble-corner-set logic is shared."},"495":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-47","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#consequences","content":"The marker side length on the Mongolian-standard preset bumps from `0.02` to\n`0.04` (normalized) so the printed marker has enough cells of margin to remain\ndetectable after a copier round-trip."},"496":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers-48","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0009-aruco-markers#follow-up","content":"Real-scan validation lands in P8 hardening once we have representative MFP and\nphone fixtures from a partner school. Until then, the synthetic fixtures in\n`crates/shalgalt-cv/tests/fixtures/` (P3-09) lock the ArUco detection path\nagainst regressions."},"497":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","type":"page","content":"ADR 0010 — Fill measurement & confidence","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band"},"498":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","content":"Per-bubble fill scoring on the warped canvas, the confidence formula, and the locked [0.35, 0.65] needs-review bands."},"499":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#context","content":"Context"},"500":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--measurement","content":"Decision — measurement"},"501":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Decision — confidence"},"502":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--band-thresholds","content":"Decision — band thresholds"},"503":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"504":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"505":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#context","content":"Once the page is warped to a canonical canvas (ADR 0009), the CV pipeline must turn\neach bubble into a single `(fill, confidence)` reading. The grading engine\n(`crates/shalgalt-core/src/grading/engine.rs`) already implements the consumer side:\nit expects a `BubbleReading { group_id, bubble_index, fill, confidence }` per bubble\nand classifies them into the `[<0.35, 0.35..=0.65, >0.65]` bands."},"506":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#context","content":"Two engineering questions remain:"},"507":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#context","content":"How do we measure `fill` from the warped image?"},"508":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#context","content":"What does `confidence` mean, and how is it computed?"},"509":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--measurement","content":"For each bubble:"},"510":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--measurement","content":"Convert the bubble's normalized centre to canvas pixel coordinates against the\nwarped canonical image (1700 × 2400 px)."},"511":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--measurement","content":"Sample a disc of radius `BUBBLE_RADIUS_FRACTION × canvas_width = 0.010 × 1700 ≈\n17 px`. The bubble itself is printed at radius `0.012 × canvas_width ≈ 20 px`,\nso the sample disc is strictly inside the printed circle and never picks up\nthe ring stroke."},"512":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--measurement","content":"Compute `fill = mean(255 − gray) / 255` inside the sample disc, where `gray` is\nthe warped 8U grayscale image. Result is in `[0, 1]`."},"513":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--measurement","content":"We **do not** apply adaptive thresholding before measurement, even though\nadaptive thresholding is the right preprocessing for line-art / outline detection\nelsewhere in the pipeline. The reason is documented in\n`crates/shalgalt-cv/src/threshold.rs`: a 41-pixel-block adaptive Gaussian\nthreshold tracks the local mean, and a uniformly filled disc raises the local\nmean enough that the *centre* of the disc falls below threshold and is classified\nas paper. The continuous `255 − gray` signal preserves the disc's mean intensity,\nso a fully filled bubble reads ≈ 1.0 instead of ≈ 0.05."},"514":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--measurement","content":"We **do** apply adaptive thresholding for the structural pre-warp pass\n(`threshold::binarize`) used by the Hough deskew (ADR 0009 follow-up: `deskew.rs`).\nAdaptive thresholding is the right tool when the input is text, a bubble outline,\nor any thin line-art structure that an MFP scan can degrade."},"515":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`confidence(fill) = clamp(2 × |fill − 0.5|, 0, 1)`."},"516":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Boundary readings:"},"517":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`fill`"},"518":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`confidence`"},"519":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Meaning"},"520":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`0.00`"},"521":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`1.00`"},"522":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Solidly empty paper — no doubt."},"523":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`0.35`"},"524":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`0.30`"},"525":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Lower band edge — entering uncertain territory."},"526":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`0.50`"},"527":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`0.00`"},"528":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Half-filled — equiprobable; the manual reviewer must decide."},"529":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`0.65`"},"530":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`0.30`"},"531":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Upper band edge."},"532":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`1.00`"},"533":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"`1.00`"},"534":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Solidly filled — no doubt."},"535":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--confidence","content":"Confidence is **not** consumed by the grading engine today. The engine owns the\n`fill ∈ [0.35, 0.65] ⇒ Uncertain ⇒ needs_review` rule and that decision is\ndeterministic and band-driven, not confidence-driven (see\n`crates/shalgalt-core/src/grading/engine.rs` lines 53–66 for the implementation\nreference). Confidence exists for the **manual-review queue** (P3-07): when a\nsheet has multiple uncertain bubbles, the queue surfaces low-confidence bubbles\nfirst so the reviewer can clear the most ambiguous answers fastest."},"536":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--band-thresholds","content":"The `[<0.35, 0.35..=0.65, >0.65]` bands are inherited from\n`crates/shalgalt-core/src/domain/parsed.rs`'s\n`BubbleReading::FILL_UNFILLED_MAX = 0.35` and `FILL_FILLED_MIN = 0.65` constants.\nBoth boundaries are inclusive on the *uncertain* side per the existing grading-\nengine tests:"},"537":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#decision--band-thresholds","content":"This ADR locks the bands; reopening requires a new ADR plus a master-plan update."},"538":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#consequences","content":"`crates/shalgalt-cv/src/bubbles.rs` reads from the bg-subtracted \"ink density\"\nsignal exposed as `threshold::flatten_to_ink`, not from the adaptive-threshold\nbinary. The two threshold variants share a single module and the doc string\non `binarize` calls out the reason."},"539":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#consequences","content":"`BUBBLE_RADIUS_FRACTION = 0.010` is calibrated against the Mongolian-standard\npreset's printed bubble radius (`0.012` normalized). Templates with\nsignificantly different bubble dimensions need a per-template override or a\ntemplate-aware sampling radius (out of scope for P3; revisit in P8 hardening)."},"540":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#consequences","content":"The synthetic fixtures in `crates/shalgalt-cv/tests/fixtures/` (P3-09) drive\n`fill > 0.65` for filled bubbles and `fill < 0.35` for empty bubbles in the\nclean-MFP path, validating the band boundaries end-to-end."},"541":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#follow-up","content":"Real-scan calibration in P8 hardening will tune `BUBBLE_RADIUS_FRACTION` and\nmay revisit the band thresholds against an empirical distribution of fill\nratios from real student answers."},"542":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0010-confidence-band#follow-up","content":"Per-bubble confidence is consumed by the manual-review queue (P3-07). The\nordering rule (`asc_by_confidence`) lands with that queue's UI."},"543":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","type":"page","content":"ADR 0011 — `.shalgalt` project file","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format"},"544":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","content":"A zip container with an always-plaintext manifest, streaming read/write, and a fixed internal layout for exam projects."},"545":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#context","content":"Context"},"546":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"547":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#decision","content":"Decision"},"548":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"549":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"550":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#context","content":"A teacher's exam project is not a single file. It is a template (the `OmrTemplate`, Rule 3),\none answer key per variant, free-form metadata (school, subject, exam date), an optional\nstudent roster, and optionally the original test-paper PDF. Master plan §2 calls for sharing\na whole project between teachers across machines as **one** artifact — \"juggling multiple\nfiles\" is one of the pain points the product exists to remove (§4)."},"551":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#context","content":"We need a container format that:"},"552":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#context","content":"Bundles many heterogeneous files into one."},"553":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#context","content":"Can be **previewed** (title, exam date, sheet count) without opening or decrypting the\nwhole thing — the dashboard and the import dialog show project cards."},"554":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#context","content":"Streams. A project can carry hundreds of MB of scanned PDFs; Rule 1 (\"IPC Memory Mirage\nAvoidance\") forbids loading large payloads whole, and that discipline must extend to the\narchive layer or it is pointless."},"555":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#context","content":"Is inspectable with off-the-shelf tools when unencrypted, so a stuck teacher (or a support\nengineer) can open it without our app."},"556":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Option"},"557":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Bundles many files"},"558":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Cheap metadata preview"},"559":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Streaming read/write"},"560":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Off-the-shelf inspectable"},"561":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Notes"},"562":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Single JSON blob (base64 the PDF inside)"},"563":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"564":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"no — must parse the whole blob"},"565":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"no — whole file in memory"},"566":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"poor (giant base64)"},"567":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Violates Rule 1 outright."},"568":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"SQLite file as the container"},"569":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"570":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes (a metadata table)"},"571":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"partial (blob streaming is awkward)"},"572":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"needs a SQLite viewer"},"573":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Overkill; we already have a SQLite *app* DB and do not want a second schema to version."},"574":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"`tar` archive"},"575":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"576":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"no — no central directory; must scan sequentially"},"577":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"578":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"579":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Cannot seek to the manifest; preview means reading from the front."},"580":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"**zip archive**"},"581":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"582":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"**yes — central directory + a named `manifest.json`**"},"583":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"**yes — per-entry `Read`/`Write`**"},"584":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"**yes — every OS has a zip viewer**"},"585":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Chosen."},"586":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Custom binary format"},"587":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"588":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"589":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"yes"},"590":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"no — bespoke tooling"},"591":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-47","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#options-considered","content":"Reinvents zip with no upside and a parser to maintain."},"592":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-48","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#decision","content":"Key sub-decisions:"},"593":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-49","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#decision","content":"**`manifest.json` is always plaintext**, even when the rest of the archive is encrypted\n(see 0012). It is the only entry a reader may buffer whole — it\nis tiny. It MUST NOT contain student PII, because anyone can read it without the passphrase.\nIts required keys are `format_version`, `title`, `created_at` (RFC 3339), `sheet_count`,\n`encrypted`; `exam_id` and `hint` are optional."},"594":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-50","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#decision","content":"**No custom magic header.** zip's own `PK\\x03\\x04` signature plus the `.shalgalt` extension\nis sufficient to recognize the format. A custom prefix would break \"opens in any zip viewer.\""},"595":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-51","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#decision","content":"**`format_version` integer gates forward compatibility.** A loader refuses any manifest whose\n`format_version` exceeds the version it understands, returning the stable code\n`fileformat.version_too_new`. The check runs immediately after the manifest is parsed, before\nany decryption — a future-format file fails with a precise reason rather than a confusing\ncrypto or zip error."},"596":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-52","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#decision","content":"**Streaming is mandatory (Rule 1).** The `shalgalt-fileformat` crate exposes a `write` that\ntakes an iterator of `(name, ReadHandle)` and an `open` that returns a lending iterator\n(`EntryIter::next_entry`) yielding one borrowed `ReadHandle` at a time. Nothing but the\nmanifest is ever held whole in memory. `ReadHandle::from_path` lets a caller feed a\nmulti-hundred-MB `exam.pdf` straight from disk."},"597":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-53","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#decision","content":"**Compression policy:** small plaintext JSON/CSV is DEFLATE-compressed; entries that do not\nbenefit (already-compressed PDFs, and high-entropy age ciphertext) are `Stored`. flate2's\npure-Rust `zlib-rs` backend is used so there is no system C `zlib` build dependency."},"598":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-54","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#consequences","content":"A new pure-Rust crate `crates/shalgalt-fileformat` owns read/write. It depends on `zip`\n(no default features — the bzip2/zstd/xz/aes C codecs are dropped) and, for the encrypted\ncase, `age`. It deliberately does **not** depend on `shalgalt-core`: it streams opaque named\nbyte blobs and stays domain-agnostic, so the `OmrTemplate`/`AnswerKey` types remain solely\nin `shalgalt-core::domain`."},"599":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-55","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#consequences","content":"The public API is a set of free functions (`open`, `open_manifest_only`, `write`) plus\n`Manifest` and `ReadHandle`, rather than a `ProjectFile` facade. The earlier placeholder doc\nsketched `ProjectFile::open/write`; the free-function shape is simpler for every P4 caller\nand the Tauri command layer (P4-03) builds its own domain helpers on top. A facade can be\nadded later without breaking these signatures."},"600":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-56","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#consequences","content":"Entry names are validated against zip-slip (absolute paths, `..`, backslashes) on both the\nwrite and read paths; `open` resolves names via `enclosed_name` and rejects anything unsafe."},"601":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-57","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#consequences","content":"The desktop command layer (P4-03) maps `FileFormatError::code()` to the Mongolian string\ntable the same way it already maps `AppError::code`."},"602":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-58","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#follow-up","content":"0012 records the optional `age` passphrase encryption layered on\ntop of this container."},"603":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-59","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#follow-up","content":"P4-03 wires `project_open` / `project_save` / `project_export` Tauri commands onto this\ncrate and adds the `$lib/ipc/project.ts` frontend wrapper."},"604":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-60","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#follow-up","content":"P4-07 registers the `.shalgalt` extension with the OS so a double-click opens the app."},"605":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format-61","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0011-shalgalt-file-format#follow-up","content":"A future `format_version: 2` (if the layout ever changes) must ship with a migration note and\na loader that still reads version 1."},"606":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","type":"page","content":"ADR 0012 — Optional age encryption","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption"},"607":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","content":"Passphrase-based, ASCII-armored age encryption applied per-entry to .shalgalt payloads, leaving the manifest readable."},"608":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#context","content":"Context"},"609":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"610":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#decision","content":"Decision"},"611":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"612":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"613":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#context","content":"A `.shalgalt` project bundles student-identifying data: a roster (`students.csv`) and graded\nresults tied to names. When a teacher emails a project, drops it on a shared drive, or carries\nit on a USB stick, that PII is exposed. We want **optional** at-rest encryption so a teacher can\nprotect a project with a passphrase, while keeping unencrypted projects trivially inspectable\nfor the common case."},"614":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#context","content":"Constraints:"},"615":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#context","content":"**Passphrase, not key files.** Teachers are non-technical (master plan §7, \"design for older\nteachers\"). Asking them to manage X25519 key pairs is a non-starter. A single passphrase they\nchoose and remember is the only usable model."},"616":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#context","content":"**The manifest must stay readable.** Per 0011, the dashboard\npreviews `manifest.json` without a passphrase. So encryption must be **per-entry**, wrapping\nevery file *except* the manifest — not a whole-archive blob."},"617":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#context","content":"**Streaming (Rule 1).** Encrypting a hundred-MB PDF must not buffer it in memory."},"618":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#context","content":"**Portability.** A project may travel between machines, mail systems, and zip viewers that\nmangle raw binary. The ciphertext should survive text-oriented transports."},"619":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#context","content":"**No hand-rolled crypto.** Repo security policy: never invent crypto; use a vetted library."},"620":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Option"},"621":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Passphrase UX"},"622":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Per-entry"},"623":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Streaming"},"624":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Portable encoding"},"625":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Library maturity"},"626":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Zip's built-in ZipCrypto"},"627":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"passphrase"},"628":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"per-entry"},"629":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"yes"},"630":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"n/a (in-zip)"},"631":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"**broken** — ZipCrypto is cryptographically weak."},"632":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"Zip AES (WinZip AE-2)"},"633":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"passphrase"},"634":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"per-entry"},"635":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"yes"},"636":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"n/a (in-zip)"},"637":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"OK, but couples crypto to the zip layer and ties us to one zip crate's AES feature + C deps."},"638":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"`age` with **passphrase (scrypt) recipient**"},"639":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"passphrase"},"640":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"per-entry (we wrap each entry)"},"641":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"**yes — chunked `StreamWriter`/`StreamReader`**"},"642":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"**yes — ASCII armor**"},"643":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"mature (str4d/rage), audited format. Chosen."},"644":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"`age` with X25519 key recipients"},"645":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"key files (bad UX)"},"646":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"per-entry"},"647":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"yes"},"648":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"yes"},"649":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"rejected — violates constraint 1."},"650":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"libsodium secretstream"},"651":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"passphrase (+ KDF we wire)"},"652":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"per-entry"},"653":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"yes"},"654":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-47","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"no (raw binary)"},"655":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-48","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"more wiring, less standard than age."},"656":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-49","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"GPG symmetric"},"657":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-50","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"passphrase"},"658":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-51","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"per-entry"},"659":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-52","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"yes"},"660":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-53","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"yes (armor)"},"661":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-54","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#options-considered","content":"heavy dependency, awkward Rust story."},"662":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-55","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#decision","content":"Concretely:"},"663":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-56","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#decision","content":"**What is encrypted:** every zip entry *except* `manifest.json`. `manifest.encrypted = true`\nrecords the choice so a reader knows a passphrase is required for content (but not for the\npreview)."},"664":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-57","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#decision","content":"**Passphrase handling:** the passphrase is carried as `age::secrecy::SecretString` (the\nzeroizing wrapper age re-exports — we do not add a separate `secrecy` dependency, keeping the\nversion in lockstep). Encryption uses `age::Encryptor::with_user_passphrase`; decryption uses\n`age::scrypt::Identity`."},"665":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-58","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#decision","content":"**ASCII armor always on** (master plan §6.3). Encrypted entries are written through\n`age::armor::ArmoredWriter` (`Format::AsciiArmor`) and read through `ArmoredReader`. The cost\nis a \\~33 % size increase from base64; the benefit is that ciphertext survives text-oriented\ntransports and is recognizable (`-----BEGIN AGE ENCRYPTED FILE-----`). Because armored\nciphertext is high-entropy base64, encrypted entries are `Stored` (not DEFLATEd) in the zip."},"666":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-59","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#decision","content":"**Streaming (Rule 1):** the write path pipes plaintext → `Encryptor` `StreamWriter` →\n`ArmoredWriter` → the current zip entry, and the read path reverses it, both via `io::copy`.\nNo entry is buffered whole. The age stream is closed inside-out — finish the `StreamWriter`\n(flush the final ciphertext chunk), then finish the `ArmoredWriter` (emit the armor footer);\nskipping the second finish silently truncates the armor."},"667":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-60","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#decision","content":"**Wrong-passphrase is a typed error.** A wrong passphrase fails at decrypt time. age 0.11\nsurfaces this as `DecryptError::DecryptionFailed` for a scrypt file (verified against the\ncrate — *not* `NoMatchingKeys`, which the initial research assumed; with scrypt the passphrase\nis the only key, so an unwrap failure is a decryption failure). The crate maps\n`DecryptionFailed`, `KeyDecryptionFailed`, and `NoMatchingKeys` all to a single fieldless\n`FileFormatError::BadPassphrase` (stable code `fileformat.bad_passphrase`). The variant is\nfieldless on purpose so a wrong-passphrase attempt cannot leak age internals into a log or a\nuser-facing message."},"668":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-61","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#consequences","content":"`crates/shalgalt-fileformat/src/crypto.rs` is the **only** module that touches the `age` API.\nThe rest of the crate stays crypto-library-agnostic; a future algorithm change is confined to\none file."},"669":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-62","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#consequences","content":"The `age` dependency is added with the non-default `armor` feature. Its transitive footprint\n(x25519-dalek, scrypt, etc.) is accepted as the cost of not hand-rolling crypto."},"670":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-63","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#consequences","content":"`scrypt` work factor is auto-calibrated by age to \\~1 second on the encrypting device. A file\nproduced on a fast machine and opened on a slow one could trip age's `ExcessiveWork` guard;\nthe crate maps that to a sanitized internal `Crypto` variant rather than `BadPassphrase`, so it\nis never mislabeled as a wrong passphrase. At the stable-code level `Crypto` folds into\n`fileformat.malformed` (the locked code set stays five values), so the desktop layer cannot\ntoday distinguish \"device too slow\" from \"corrupt archive\" by code alone — both surface as\n`fileformat.malformed`. If that UX distinction is ever needed, a sixth stable code can be added\nin a follow-up (and recorded here)."},"671":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-64","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#consequences","content":"**Passphrase recovery is impossible by design.** There is no escrow, no recovery key, no\nbackdoor. A lost passphrase means a lost project. The optional `manifest.hint` field exists to\nreduce that risk; it MUST NOT contain the passphrase itself. The desktop UI (P4-03/04) must\nwarn the teacher of this at the point they set a passphrase."},"672":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-65","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#consequences","content":"No passphrase is ever persisted by this crate. The desktop layer decides whether to hold it in\nmemory for a session; it is never written to disk or the SQLite DB."},"673":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-66","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#follow-up","content":"P4-03 surfaces the passphrase prompt and the \"passphrase cannot be recovered\" warning in the\nTauri command layer + frontend."},"674":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption-67","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0012-age-encryption#follow-up","content":"The \"encrypted entry's on-disk bytes never contain a plaintext substring of the payload\"\nassertion (originally slated for P8 hardening) is already covered by\n`tests/roundtrip.rs::encrypted_archive_contains_no_payload_plaintext`, which guards against an\naccidental bypass of the encrypt path."},"675":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","type":"page","content":"ADR 0013 — REST `/v1` & DataStore seam","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore"},"676":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","content":"Versioned /v1 routes, a database-free DataStore trait in core, and OpenAPI generated from utoipa annotations."},"677":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#context","content":"Context"},"678":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#decision","content":"Decision"},"679":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"680":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"681":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#context","content":"Master plan §6.6 and §8.2 call for a versioned HTTP API exposing exams, templates, and\ngraded results, reachable identically from inside the Tauri app (`127.0.0.1`, no auth) and\nfrom a standalone server (`0.0.0.0`, bearer auth). The router already lives in\n`shalgalt-core` (Rule 4) but, before P5, served only `/healthz`."},"682":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#context","content":"Two constraints shape the design:"},"683":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#context","content":"**Core is database-free.** `crates/shalgalt-core/CLAUDE.md` forbids any DB on the core\ndependency path; §8.2 pins core's dependencies to `serde`, `thiserror`, `anyhow`,\n`axum`, `tower-http`. The router must reach persistence without core knowing what the\npersistence *is*."},"684":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#context","content":"**Two hosts, one contract.** The desktop and the server must return byte-identical\nresponses for the same data (master plan §10 P5 acceptance), so the endpoint logic\ncannot be duplicated per host."},"685":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#decision","content":"**1. Version under `/v1/`.** All resource routes are `/v1/{exams,templates,results}`.\n`/healthz` and `/openapi.json` sit outside the version prefix (they are service metadata,\nnot part of the data contract). A breaking change to any `/v1/` shape requires a `/v2/`\nand a new ADR."},"686":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#decision","content":"**2. A `DataStore` trait is the persistence seam.** Core defines `DataStore` (object-safe,\n`Send + Sync`) plus the DTOs that cross it (`ExamDto`, `TemplateDto`, `ResultDto`, the\n`New*` request bodies). `AppState` holds an `Arc<dyn DataStore>`; every handler reads/writes\nthrough it. Core ships an in-memory `MemoryStore` for tests. Each host injects a concrete\nimplementation (see ADR 0014). Core still touches no database."},"687":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#decision","content":"**3. DTOs are separate from `domain::*`.** The wire shapes are their own types so the REST\ncontract can evolve without dragging the grading/IPC models. Opaque payloads\n(`templates.json_schema`, `results.detail_answers`) are passed through as strings — the API\nnever reshapes the Rule 3 template format."},"688":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#decision","content":"**4. OpenAPI via `utoipa`, served at `/openapi.json`.** Handlers carry `#[utoipa::path]` and\nDTOs derive `ToSchema`, so the spec is generated from the same annotations that wire the\nroutes and cannot drift. `utoipa` is added to core as the single OpenAPI dependency\n(sanctioned by §8.2's `api::router` surface). No Swagger UI is bundled — this is an\noffline-first product; consumers point their own tooling at the JSON."},"689":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#decision","content":"**5. Errors reuse the IPC envelope.** `AppError` gains an axum `IntoResponse` that emits the\nexisting `{ code, message }` body with a derived status (`BadRequest` → 400, `NotFound` →\n404, else 500), so REST clients and the Tauri frontend read identical error shapes."},"690":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#consequences","content":"The router is testable in-process over `MemoryStore` (no socket, no database) — see the\n`api` tests in core."},"691":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#consequences","content":"Adding an endpoint means: a `DataStore` method, a handler with `#[utoipa::path]`, a route\nline, and a `paths(...)` entry. The OpenAPI document updates itself."},"692":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#consequences","content":"`read_only()` is a shared `BadRequest` the desktop's read-only store returns for `create_*`\n— write endpoints exist in the contract but are rejected in local mode (see ADR 0014)."},"693":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#consequences","content":"`?exam_id=` on `/v1/results` filters the new `results.exam_id` column (migration 0005),\nso the spec's filter is a real column predicate rather than an approximation."},"694":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#follow-up","content":"Pagination on `/v1/results` is deferred until result volumes justify it; today the desktop\nbrowser paginates client-side."},"695":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0013-rest-api-v1-datastore#follow-up","content":"A future `/v2/` (if ever needed) keeps `/v1/` alive for one release for integrators."},"696":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","type":"page","content":"ADR 0014 — Standalone server & rusqlite store","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store"},"697":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","content":"A shared rusqlite DataStore implementation, with the desktop's read path split from plugin-sql writes."},"698":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#context","content":"Context"},"699":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"700":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"Decision"},"701":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"702":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"703":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#context","content":"ADR 0013 leaves persistence to a host-injected `DataStore`. Two hosts need one:\n`apps/server` (a headless LAN deployment) and `apps/desktop` (the embedded API). The\ndesktop is the hard case: its SQLite file is owned by `tauri-plugin-sql&#x60; (sqlx), and the\nrepo rule is &#x2A;*\"no DB writes in Rust — plugin-sql is the single writer\"**\n(`apps/desktop/CLAUDE.md`). Core must stay database-free (§8.2), so the rusqlite code cannot\nlive there."},"704":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#context","content":"Where should the concrete store live, and how does the desktop read SQLite without becoming\na second writer?"},"705":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"Question"},"706":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"Option"},"707":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"Verdict"},"708":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"Where does the rusqlite impl live?"},"709":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"In core behind a feature"},"710":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — violates §8.2's \"core depends only on serde/thiserror/anyhow/axum/tower-http\"."},"711":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"Duplicated in each host"},"712":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — DRY; \\~250 lines of SQL drift between two binaries."},"713":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"A shared `crates/shalgalt-store`"},"714":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — one impl, both hosts depend on it, core stays clean."},"715":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"How does the desktop read?"},"716":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"A read-write rusqlite connection"},"717":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — two writers on one file; breaks the single-writer rule."},"718":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"A read-only rusqlite connection"},"719":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — `SQLITE_OPEN_READ_ONLY`; cannot write, so plugin-sql stays the only writer."},"720":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"Server CLI vs env"},"721":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"All env vars"},"722":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — master plan §6.6 specifies `--bind`/`--db`/`--allow-origin`."},"723":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"CLI flags + token in env"},"724":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — flags for config, `SHALGALT_API_TOKEN` in env (a secret belongs in env, not argv)."},"725":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"**1. New crate `crates/shalgalt-store`.** It depends on `shalgalt-core` (for the trait +\nDTOs) and `rusqlite` (`bundled`), and exports `SqliteStore` implementing `DataStore`, plus\na `DeferredReadOnlyStore` for the desktop. Workspace §8.1/§8.2 is updated to list it."},"726":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"**2. Two postures.**"},"727":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"`open_read_only(path)` — desktop. Opens `SQLITE_OPEN_READ_ONLY`; `create_*` returns the\ncore read-only error. The API read path is **separate from the plugin-sql write\nownership**: plugin-sql remains the single source of truth for writes, the API only reads."},"728":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"`open_read_write(path)` + `migrate()` — server. Owns the whole file (WAL), serves the full\nread/write surface."},"729":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"**3. The desktop reader is deferred.** `tauri-plugin-sql` creates the SQLite file lazily (on\nthe frontend's first `Database.load`), which is *after* the embedded server boots.\n`DeferredReadOnlyStore` opens a fresh read-only connection per request and reports an empty\ndatabase until the file exists, so boot never fails on a missing file. Traffic is local and\nlow-volume, so per-request connection setup is acceptable."},"730":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"**4. One schema source of truth.** `migrate()` applies the desktop's `migrations/*.sql`,\nembedded by relative path via `include_str!`. It is bootstrap-only (no-op if `templates`\nalready exists), so the server can stand up a fresh database with the exact DDL the desktop\nuses, while schema *evolution* on a shared file stays owned by plugin-sql's migration chain."},"731":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"**5. SQLite linkage.** `rusqlite`'s `bundled` feature links the same vendored SQLite that\nsqlx (`libsqlite3-sys`) already pulls into the desktop binary; cargo unifies them into one\nSQLite rather than two."},"732":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#decision","content":"**6. Server assembly is a library.** `apps/server` is split `lib.rs` (CLI + `build_app` +\n`serve`) / `main.rs` so the auth path is integration-testable via `tower::oneshot` without\nbinding a socket. Layer order: auth inside CORS, so the CORS preflight (`OPTIONS`, no\n`Authorization`) is answered before the bearer guard."},"733":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#consequences","content":"The same `/v1/` data is served inside Tauri and from the server (P5 acceptance met), with\none store implementation."},"734":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#consequences","content":"The desktop's \"no DB writes in Rust\" rule holds: the carve-out is a *pure reader*, all SQL\nconfined to `shalgalt-store`. `apps/desktop/AGENTS.md` records the carve-out."},"735":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#consequences","content":"`AppDirs::db_path()` was corrected to resolve against `app_config_dir` — where\n`tauri-plugin-sql` actually writes — not `app_data_dir` (the prior \"reference only\" value\nwas wrong and never exercised)."},"736":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#consequences","content":"Two SQLite access layers (sqlx writer, rusqlite reader) coexist; readers never block the\nwriter in SQLite, and a 5 s `busy_timeout` absorbs brief contention."},"737":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#follow-up","content":"A bundled Release asset for `shalgalt-server` lands in P6 (`release.yml`)."},"738":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#follow-up","content":"Token rotation for server mode is documented but not yet automated."},"739":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#follow-up","content":"**Blocking I/O on the async executor.** `DataStore` methods are synchronous and run\ndirectly inside the axum handlers, and `SqliteStore` serializes them through one\n`Mutex<Connection>`. For the desktop (single user) and a small-school LAN server (low\nconcurrency, WAL reads) this is acceptable. If concurrency grows, offload the calls with\n`tokio::task::spawn_blocking` (or make `DataStore` async) and/or use a connection pool so\na slow query cannot park a worker thread. Deferred until measured load justifies it."},"740":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0014-server-binary-and-rusqlite-store#follow-up","content":"**Pagination.** List endpoints are currently unbounded (see ADR 0013 — the desktop\nbrowser paginates client-side). A server-enforced page-size cap on `/v1/results` lands\nwhen result volumes warrant it."},"741":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","type":"page","content":"ADR 0015 — API port & fallback","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback"},"742":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","content":"An uncommon default port (22345), desktop auto-fallback, and a developer environment override."},"743":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#context","content":"Context"},"744":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"745":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#decision","content":"Decision"},"746":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"747":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"748":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#context","content":"P5 introduced two hosts that bind a TCP port: the desktop's embedded API (loopback) and the\nstandalone `shalgalt-server` (LAN). Both originally hard-coded port **8080**."},"749":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#context","content":"8080 is one of the most contended ports on a developer or teacher machine — Tomcat,\nJenkins, countless dev servers, and corporate proxies all default to it. Worse, the desktop\nbinder had two failure problems when 8080 was taken:"},"750":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#context","content":"**Not configurable.** The port was a hard-coded literal; a teacher had no way to move it."},"751":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#context","content":"**A bind failure bricked the whole app, silently.** `api::spawn(...).await?` propagated\nthe error out of `bootstrap`, which &#x2A;skipped the subsequent `app.manage(state)`*. The\nwindow still opened, but every IPC command that needs `State<AppState>` (scanning, PDF\ngeneration, xlsx export) then failed — with nothing but one line in the log file. A\nsingle port collision turned the app into a silent brick."},"752":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#context","content":"The standalone server failed more gracefully (it exits with a clear error and `--bind` is\nalready configurable), but shared the contended default."},"753":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Question"},"754":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Option"},"755":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Verdict"},"756":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Keep 8080?"},"757":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Yes, document the collision risk"},"758":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — the risk is real on the exact machines we target (school PCs) and the failure mode is catastrophic."},"759":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"New default port"},"760":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"A common alt (8000/8888/9000)"},"761":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — equally contended."},"762":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"A registered-range, uncommon port"},"763":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Chosen — 22345.** In the IANA *registered* range (1024–49151) so the OS never hands it out as an ephemeral port, IANA-unassigned, and nowhere near common dev defaults."},"764":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"An OS-assigned ephemeral port (`:0`)"},"765":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Rejected as the default** — integrators want a stable, documentable port; pure ephemeral makes discovery mandatory every run."},"766":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Desktop behavior when the port is busy"},"767":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Hard fail"},"768":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — the embedded API is an *optional* integration surface; the app must keep working without it."},"769":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Auto-fallback to the next free port"},"770":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — try `[desired, desired+16)`, bind the first free one, and *isolate the failure* so `app.manage(state)` always runs."},"771":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Server behavior when the port is busy"},"772":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Auto-fallback"},"773":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — a LAN server advertises a fixed port to clients; silently moving it would strand them. Hard fail so the operator picks another `--bind`."},"774":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"How integrators discover the bound port (after fallback)"},"775":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Endpoint file + IPC command"},"776":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — the desktop writes `app_data_dir/api-endpoint.json` (`{ port, base_url }`) and exposes an `api_info` command."},"777":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Developer port override"},"778":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"New CLI flag"},"779":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Rejected for desktop** — it has no CLI; the server already has `--bind`."},"780":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"Environment variable"},"781":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#options-considered","content":"**Chosen — `SHALGALT_API_PORT`** for the desktop. It is a developer knob (not user-facing UI), so it does not touch the Mongolian-only UI rule."},"782":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#decision","content":"**1. Default port → 22345**, for both hosts. Desktop binds `127.0.0.1:22345`; the server's\n`--bind` default becomes `0.0.0.0:22345`."},"783":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#decision","content":"**2. Desktop auto-fallback.** `api::spawn` resolves a *desired* port (from\n`SHALGALT_API_PORT`, else 22345) and binds the first free port in `[desired, desired+16)`.\nOnly `AddrInUse` triggers fallback; other bind errors return immediately so a real\nmisconfiguration is not masked. The chosen port rides along in `ApiHandle::port()`."},"784":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#decision","content":"**3. Failure isolation (the bug fix).** `bootstrap` now `match`es on `api::spawn`: on\nsuccess it manages the handle and an `ApiInfo::running(port)`; on failure it logs and\nmanages `ApiInfo::disabled()&#x60;. **`app.manage(state)` always runs**, so a missing API never\nbreaks IPC."},"785":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#decision","content":"**4. Discovery.** On a successful bind the desktop writes `api-endpoint.json`\n(`{ \"port\", \"base_url\" }`) into the app data dir and exposes an `api_info` IPC command\nreturning `{ running, port, base_url }`. Integrators read either instead of assuming 8080."},"786":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#decision","content":"**5. Developer override.** `SHALGALT_API_PORT` pins the desktop's starting port (fallback\nstill applies). The server keeps `--bind` for explicit control and does **not** fall back."},"787":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#consequences","content":"A teacher whose machine already runs something on 22345 gets a working app on 22346+,\nwith the real port discoverable from `api-endpoint.json`. No silent brick."},"788":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#consequences","content":"External integrations must stop hard-coding 8080. The endpoint file + `api_info` command\nare the supported discovery paths."},"789":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-47","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#consequences","content":"The server's behavior is intentionally stricter than the desktop's: identical default\nport, but no fallback. This asymmetry is documented in both `AGENTS.md` files."},"790":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-48","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#consequences","content":"BLUEPRINT §2 and master plan §6.6 are updated in the same PR (both now point here)."},"791":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-49","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#follow-up","content":"When a developer-settings surface lands, show `api_info` (port + base URL) there so users\ncan copy the integration endpoint without opening the data dir."},"792":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback-50","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0015-api-port-default-and-fallback#follow-up","content":"Consider a server-side `--port-fallback` opt-in if headless deployments ever want it; not\nneeded today."},"793":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","type":"page","content":"ADR 0016 — Partial-marker homography","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography"},"794":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","content":"Recover perspective from 3 of 4 ArUco markers using per-corner correspondences and RANSAC."},"795":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#context","content":"Context"},"796":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"797":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#decision","content":"Decision"},"798":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"799":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"800":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#context","content":"ADR 0009 adopted four `DICT_6X6_50` ArUco markers (IDs 0..3, TL/TR/BR/BL) as the\nperspective-alignment fiducials. The original `perspective.rs` implementation reduced\neach detected marker to its **centre point** (averaging the four corners the detector\nreturns) and then solved an exact perspective transform with\n`getPerspectiveTransform`, which consumes exactly four point correspondences."},"801":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#context","content":"That made all four markers mandatory: a planar homography has 8 degrees of freedom and\nneeds four point pairs, so one marker per correspondence means four markers or nothing.\nIn practice the single most common reason a hand-photographed or photocopied sheet fails\nalignment is **one** corner being lost to glare, shadow, a fold, or cropping — and the\n\"all four required\" rule turned that recoverable situation into a hard failure."},"802":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#context","content":"The four-marker requirement was never a mathematical necessity; it was a consequence of\nthrowing away 12 of the 16 corner points the detector already provides."},"803":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"Option"},"804":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"Min markers to align"},"805":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"Robustness to one lost corner"},"806":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"Notes"},"807":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"Keep centres + `getPerspectiveTransform` (status quo)"},"808":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"4"},"809":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"none — hard fail"},"810":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"4 correspondences, exact fit"},"811":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"Centres + `findHomography`"},"812":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"4"},"813":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"none (still 1 pt/marker)"},"814":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"least-squares but still needs 4 markers"},"815":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"**Corners + `findHomography` (RANSAC), ≥3 markers**"},"816":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"3"},"817":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"recovers one lost marker"},"818":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"12–16 correspondences, over-determined"},"819":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"Corners + `findHomography`, ≥2 markers"},"820":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"2"},"821":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"recovers two"},"822":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#options-considered","content":"two markers on one edge are degenerate / unstable"},"823":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#decision","content":"Each detected marker contributes 4 correspondences, so three markers give 12 points\nspanning three page corners — well-conditioned for a perspective fit. Four markers give\n16 points; RANSAC additionally discards a single mis-located corner."},"824":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#decision","content":"The corner ordering returned by ArUco (clockwise from the marker's own top-left,\n`[TL, TR, BR, BL]`) matches the destination corner order computed from the template, so\ncorrespondences line up by index. Because every marker is printed upright, this mapping\nholds for all four slots."},"825":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#decision","content":"Below three markers the homography is too poorly constrained (two markers on the same\npage edge are near-degenerate), so `< 3` remains a `BadRequest` failure."},"826":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#decision","content":"Nothing on the printed sheet changes. The corners already exist in every printed\nmarker; existing answer sheets keep working and align more reliably."},"827":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#decision","content":"Destination corner positions are computed in canonical-pixel space directly from the\ntemplate's `Marker { position, size }` — no `PaperSpec` is threaded into the CV crate.\nThe canonical canvas aspect (`WARP_OUT_W:WARP_OUT_H = 1700:2400 ≈ A4 210:297`) already\nmatches the print paper (an invariant the bubble sampler relies on), so a single square\nhalf-extent `size * 0.5 * min(WARP_OUT_W, WARP_OUT_H)` reproduces the printed marker\ngeometry to within a fraction of a pixel."},"828":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#consequences","content":"`crates/shalgalt-cv/src/perspective.rs`: `DetectedMarker` now carries `corners: [Point2f; 4]` instead of a `centre`. `detect_corner_markers` returns\n`Vec<DetectedMarker>` (the detected subset, sorted by id) and fails only below\n`MIN_MARKERS = 3`. `MarkerLayout` stores per-marker canonical-pixel corner\ndestinations. `warp_to_canonical` takes a `&[DetectedMarker]` slice and calls\n`find_homography`."},"829":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#consequences","content":"`crates/shalgalt-cv/src/pipeline.rs` is unchanged — `&Vec<DetectedMarker>` coerces to\nthe new `&[DetectedMarker]` parameter, and both call sites already pass `&markers`."},"830":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#consequences","content":"The user-facing failure copy is unchanged (still a generic \"хуудас танигдсангүй\"\ntoast); only the developer console hint (`src/lib/grade/diagnostics.ts`) is reworded to\n\"fewer than 3 of 4 markers\"."},"831":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#consequences","content":"A new integration test (`three_markers_still_align`) drops the TL marker and asserts a\nknown filled bubble still reads `> 0.65`, which also locks in the corner-ordering\ncorrespondence. `deliberately_bad` now blacks out two top markers so the\n\"fails gracefully\" assertion stays deterministic under the ≥3 rule."},"832":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#follow-up","content":"Real-scan validation in P8 hardening may revisit whether a 2-diagonal-marker case is\nworth supporting; it is intentionally excluded here to avoid degenerate fits."},"833":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0016-partial-marker-homography#follow-up","content":"`find_homography`'s RANSAC threshold (3 px) is calibrated against the 1700×2400\ncanonical canvas; P8 may tune it against representative phone/MFP fixtures."},"834":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","type":"page","content":"ADR 0017 — GitHub Releases distribution","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution"},"835":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","content":"Ship desktop bundles and the standalone server through GitHub Releases via tauri-action on v* tags."},"836":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#context","content":"Context"},"837":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"838":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#decision","content":"Decision"},"839":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"840":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#positive","content":"Positive"},"841":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#negative","content":"Negative"},"842":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"843":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#context","content":"P6 turns the workspace into shippable artifacts. Master plan §6.8/§6.9 lock the channel\n(GitHub Releases triggered by `v*` tags) and the OS priority (Windows 1, macOS 2,\nLinux 3), but leave the *how* to an ADR: which workflow drives the build, which assets\nland on a Release, and what we do without real code-signing certificates."},"844":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#context","content":"Three constraints make this non-trivial:"},"845":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#context","content":"**No signing certificates are available yet.** A real Windows EV/OV certificate and an\nApple Developer account are both pending. We cannot block the first tagged build on\nprocurement."},"846":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#context","content":"**Native runtime libraries do not statically link.** Per ADR 0001 the Windows build\nlinks `opencv_world<NNN>.dll`, and the CV pipeline also depends on a `pdfium` shared\nlibrary. Both must travel *with* the installer or the produced binary will not launch\non a clean machine."},"847":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#context","content":"**Two products ship from one tag.** The desktop bundle (NSIS + MSI) and the headless\n`shalgalt-server` binary (ADR 0014) are both v1.0 deliverables and should be published\nfrom the same Release so versions never drift."},"848":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Question"},"849":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Option"},"850":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Verdict"},"851":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Build driver"},"852":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Hand-rolled `cargo tauri build` matrix in `release.yml`"},"853":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — re-implements bundling, signing hooks, and Release upload that `tauri-action` already does."},"854":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"`tauri-apps/tauri-action`"},"855":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — official action; creates/updates the Release, builds per-OS bundles, uploads assets, and emits the `latest.json` updater manifest when configured."},"856":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Trigger"},"857":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Push to `stable`"},"858":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — couples every release-branch merge to a publish; no clean version anchor."},"859":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"`v*` tag push"},"860":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — matches master plan §6.8; the tag is the single version source of truth, and a Release is an explicit, intentional act."},"861":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Windows signing (now)"},"862":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Block release until an EV/OV cert exists"},"863":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — stalls the entire P6 milestone on a procurement timeline we do not control."},"864":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Ship a &#x2A;*self-signed `v0`** build, swap in the real cert later via secrets"},"865":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — unblocks distribution; SmartScreen warns but the artifact is installable and verifiable."},"866":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"macOS signing/notarization (now)"},"867":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Require Apple notarization"},"868":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — needs a paid Apple Developer account we do not yet have."},"869":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Notarization **optional, gated behind a flag**; skipped when no Apple secrets are present"},"870":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — produces an (unnotarized) `.dmg` for testing; flips to notarized once credentials land, no workflow rewrite."},"871":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Server binary"},"872":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Separate workflow / separate Release"},"873":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — version drift between desktop and server."},"874":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"Same Release, extra build step uploads `shalgalt-server` as an asset"},"875":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — one tag, one Release, both products in lockstep."},"876":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#decision","content":"**1. `release.yml` triggers on `v*` tags and drives `tauri-action`.** The workflow checks\nout the tag, installs the per-OS native toolchain (the OpenCV setup from ADR 0001 on\nWindows, system OpenCV on Linux/macOS), runs `pnpm build` for the SvelteKit assets, then\nhands off to `tauri-action`, which builds the bundle, attaches it to the Release, and —\nwhen the updater is configured (ADR 0018) — writes the signed `latest.json` manifest."},"877":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#decision","content":"**2. OS rollout follows master-plan priority.** Windows (NSIS + MSI) is the first and\nmandatory target. macOS (`.dmg`) and Linux (AppImage + `.deb`) jobs exist in the same\nworkflow but may be left cert-blocked / `continue-on-error` until P9 per master plan\n§6.9; the *workflow shape* is built once so enabling an OS later is a flag flip, not a\nrewrite."},"878":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#decision","content":"**3. Signing posture is staged.**"},"879":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#decision","content":"**Windows**: a **self-signed certificate** is used for the initial `v0`-class builds.\nThe signing cert/password are read from repository secrets\n(`WINDOWS_CERTIFICATE`, `WINDOWS_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD`). Swapping to a real EV/OV cert\nis a secret-value change only — the workflow does not change."},"880":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#decision","content":"**macOS**: notarization is **optional and skipped** when the Apple secrets\n(`APPLE_ID`, `APPLE_PASSWORD`, `APPLE_TEAM_ID`, signing identity) are absent. The build\nstill produces a `.dmg`; it is simply not notarized until an Apple Developer account\nexists."},"881":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#decision","content":"**4. The standalone server is a Release asset.** A dedicated build step compiles\n`apps/server` (`shalgalt-server`) for the same targets and uploads the binary (archived\nwith its license/readme) to the *same* Release created by `tauri-action`, so a tag yields\nboth the desktop installer and the headless server in one place."},"882":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-47","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#decision","content":"**5. Native runtime libraries are bundled, not assumed.** Following ADR 0001, the Windows\njob places `opencv_world<NNN>.dll` (and the `pdfium` shared library) where the bundler\nincludes them as Tauri `resources`/`externalBin` so the installed app and the server\nbinary both find their native dependencies on a clean machine."},"883":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-48","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#positive","content":"A single `v*` tag produces a complete, downloadable Release: Windows installer +\n`shalgalt-server`, with macOS/Linux ready to enable."},"884":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-49","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#positive","content":"Distribution is unblocked today despite missing certificates; the cert story is a\nsecret swap, not a code change."},"885":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-50","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#positive","content":"Versions never drift: desktop and server publish from one tag, one Release."},"886":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-51","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#positive","content":"Aligns with §6.10 — no telemetry, no update phone-home in the build pipeline itself."},"887":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-52","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#negative","content":"**Self-signed Windows builds trigger SmartScreen warnings.** Users must click through\n\"More info → Run anyway\" until a real reputation-bearing cert is installed. Documented\nin the user manual (P7)."},"888":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-53","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#negative","content":"**Unnotarized macOS `.dmg` is Gatekeeper-blocked** by default; testers must\nright-click → Open or clear the quarantine attribute. Resolved when notarization is\nswitched on."},"889":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-54","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#negative","content":"**Installer footprint carries the full native libs** (`opencv_world` \\~70 MB per\nADR 0001, plus `pdfium`). Acceptable for USB / school-network distribution; an installer\ndiet is the ADR 0001 follow-up, not a P6 blocker."},"890":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-55","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#negative","content":"**Coupled to upstream action + URL formats.** `tauri-action` and the OpenCV/pdfium\ndownload URLs are external dependencies; if they break, the workflow needs maintenance."},"891":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-56","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#follow-up","content":"**Real Windows EV/OV certificate**: procure, store as secrets, retire the self-signed\npath. SmartScreen reputation accrues afterwards."},"892":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-57","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#follow-up","content":"**Apple Developer account + notarization**: enable the notarization flag and remove the\nskip once credentials exist."},"893":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-58","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#follow-up","content":"**Linux `.deb` + AppImage hardening**: confirm the bundled `pdfium`/OpenCV resolve on\ncommon distros before flipping the Linux job from optional to required (P9)."},"894":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution-59","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0017-github-releases-distribution#follow-up","content":"**Installer diet** inherits ADR 0001's P5/P6 follow-up — feature-selective OpenCV build\nif footprint becomes a complaint vector."},"895":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","type":"page","content":"ADR 0018 — Opt-in updater","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater"},"896":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","content":"tauri-plugin-updater with a static gh-pages manifest, default OFF so offline schools never see a prompt."},"897":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#context","content":"Context"},"898":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"899":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#decision","content":"Decision"},"900":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"901":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#positive","content":"Positive"},"902":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#negative","content":"Negative"},"903":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"904":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#context","content":"Master plan §6.8 commits to `tauri-plugin-updater` for in-app updates, and §6.10 forbids\nall telemetry, crash reporting, and analytics. The product's primary user is a teacher on\nan **offline school network**. These two facts collide on a single question: an\nauto-updater is, by nature, a process that reaches out to the network on launch."},"905":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#context","content":"The hard requirements:"},"906":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#context","content":"**Offline schools must never see an update prompt.** A spinner or \"update available\"\ndialog on a machine with no internet is a support burden and erodes trust in an\noffline-first tool."},"907":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#context","content":"**No phone-home.** A version check is itself a network beacon (timestamp, IP, app\nversion). §6.10 rules out anything that smells like telemetry, so a check must only\nhappen when the user has explicitly asked for it."},"908":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#context","content":"**Updates must still be verifiable.** When a connected teacher *does* opt in, the\nmanifest and bundles must be signature-checked so a tampered update cannot install."},"909":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#context","content":"Where does the update manifest live, and what is the default behavior?"},"910":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Question"},"911":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Option"},"912":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Verdict"},"913":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Default behavior"},"914":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Auto-check on every launch (industry default)"},"915":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — violates §6.10 (silent phone-home) and shows prompts on offline machines."},"916":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Opt-in, default OFF**; teacher flips a toggle"},"917":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — no network access until explicitly enabled; offline schools stay silent."},"918":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Manifest hosting"},"919":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Dynamic update server"},"920":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — a server to run/secure, and an always-on endpoint we'd have to keep alive; over-engineered for a static artifact."},"921":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Same Release asset"},"922":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Considered** — works, but the endpoint URL changes per tag, awkward to pin."},"923":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Static JSON on the `gh-pages` branch**"},"924":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — free hosting, a stable URL, no infrastructure; matches §6.8's \"static JSON\" model."},"925":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Signature trust"},"926":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"Trust TLS / GitHub only"},"927":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Rejected** — TLS authenticates the host, not the payload; we want payload integrity independent of transport."},"928":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**`tauri-plugin-updater` minisign signatures**"},"929":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#options-considered","content":"**Chosen** — the bundle + manifest are signed with the updater keypair; the public key is compiled into the app and verifies every update."},"930":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#decision","content":"**1. The updater is opt-in and OFF by default.** `tauri-plugin-updater&#x60; is wired in, but\nno update check fires on launch. A **\"Check for updates\" toggle** lives in app\npreferences, next to the theme / comfortable-typography controls (ADR 0006). The plugin\nonly contacts the network after a teacher turns it on (or presses an explicit\n\"Check now\"). On a fresh install and on every offline machine, the app makes **zero**\nupdate-related network calls — satisfying §6.10 and the offline-school requirement."},"931":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#decision","content":"**2. The update manifest is a static `latest.json` on `gh-pages`.** The canonical endpoint\nis:"},"932":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#decision","content":"It is published by the `release.yml` workflow (ADR 0017) when a `v*` tag is built, and\ndescribes the latest version, per-platform bundle URLs (the Release assets), and their\nsignatures. No dynamic server exists; the endpoint is a flat file served by GitHub Pages."},"933":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-37","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#decision","content":"**3. Updates are signature-verified.** Bundles and the manifest are signed with the\n`tauri-plugin-updater` (minisign) keypair. The **public key is embedded in the app**\n(`tauri.conf.json` updater config); the **private key lives only in CI secrets**\n(`TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY`, `TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD`) and is never\ncommitted. The plugin refuses any update whose signature does not verify against the\nembedded public key, so transport compromise alone cannot push a malicious update."},"934":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-38","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#decision","content":"**4. UI strings follow the language rule.** The toggle label, the \"update available\" copy,\nand any error surface are **Mongolian**, referenced by key from the P1 string-table — not\nhard-coded. The updater plugin's own `AppError`-style codes stay English (stable\nidentifiers, mapped to Mongolian in the table)."},"935":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-39","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#positive","content":"**Offline schools never see a prompt.** Default-OFF means no network access until a\nteacher chooses it — the strongest possible answer to the offline-first requirement."},"936":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-40","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#positive","content":"**No telemetry / no phone-home** by default, satisfying §6.10. A version check only\nexists as a user-initiated action."},"937":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-41","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#positive","content":"**Zero update infrastructure.** A static `gh-pages` file is free, has a stable URL, and\ncannot \"go down\" the way a custom update server can."},"938":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-42","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#positive","content":"**Tamper-resistant.** Signature verification against an embedded public key protects the\nupdate path independently of TLS."},"939":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-43","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#positive","content":"**Teacher control.** Connected users who *want* updates get a clear, deliberate switch."},"940":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-44","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#negative","content":"**Most users stay on whatever they installed.** Because the default is OFF, the\npopulation skews toward old versions; security/bug fixes propagate only to opt-ins or via\nre-download. Acceptable given the offline-first, no-telemetry priorities — manual\nre-install from the Release page is always available."},"941":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-45","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#negative","content":"**Signing-key custody is critical.** Losing `TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY` means no machine\ncan verify a new update (every client trusts only the embedded public key); rotating it\nrequires shipping a new app version with the new public key first. Key backup/rotation is\na documented operational follow-up."},"942":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-46","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#negative","content":"**`gh-pages` is a single point of distribution** for the manifest. If the Pages site is\nunavailable, opt-in checks fail gracefully (no update found) — they do not block the app."},"943":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-47","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#follow-up","content":"**Signing-key backup + rotation runbook**: document where the private key is stored, how\nit is backed up, and the version-bridged rotation procedure (P7 docs)."},"944":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-48","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#follow-up","content":"**`latest.json` generation in `release.yml`**: confirm the manifest schema and per-OS\nasset URLs are emitted correctly once the macOS/Linux jobs (ADR 0017) are enabled."},"945":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-49","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#follow-up","content":"**String-table keys** for the updater UI land with the toggle implementation (P6-04)."},"946":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater-50","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0018-optin-updater#follow-up","content":"**Verify default-OFF** is asserted in the v1.0 acceptance checklist (master plan §17 —\n\"Auto-updater is **off** by default\")."},"947":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","type":"page","content":"ADR 0019 — Documentation site","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages"},"948":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","content":"Adopt Fumadocs as the single docs framework for dev docs, the Mongolian user manual, and the API reference, deployed to GitHub Pages."},"949":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#context","content":"Context"},"950":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#options-considered","content":"Options considered"},"951":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#decision","content":"Decision"},"952":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#internationalization-i18n","content":"Internationalization (i18n)"},"953":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#github-pages-coexistence-with-the-updater-manifest","content":"GitHub Pages coexistence with the updater manifest"},"954":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"955":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#context","content":"Master plan §12 originally specified two separate documentation toolchains for P7:"},"956":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#context","content":"**mdBook** for the developer documentation under `docs/dev/`."},"957":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#context","content":"**VitePress** for the Mongolian user manual under `docs/user/`."},"958":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#context","content":"A third step (P7-03) rendered the `/v1/` OpenAPI document via `redoc`."},"959":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#context","content":"Running three tools (mdBook, VitePress, redoc) means three build pipelines, three\nthemes, three search implementations, and three deploy steps. The OpenAPI page in\nparticular (`redoc`) sits awkwardly between the two sites. For a single-maintainer\nproject the operational cost of three toolchains is the dominant concern (master plan\n§19 lists \"single-maintainer bus factor\" as a tracked risk)."},"960":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#options-considered","content":"**mdBook + VitePress + redoc** (original plan). Three pipelines. mdBook is Rust-native\n(fits the crate docs story) but its theme and search are basic and it has no first-class\nOpenAPI rendering. VitePress covers the user manual well but is a second toolchain."},"961":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#options-considered","content":"**VitePress for both surfaces.** One tool, but no first-class OpenAPI rendering (would\nstill need a redoc/embed step) and weaker API-reference ergonomics."},"962":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#options-considered","content":"**Fumadocs for everything.** A single Next.js documentation framework that covers the\ndeveloper docs, the Mongolian user manual, and the HTTP API reference in one site:"},"963":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#options-considered","content":"`fumadocs-openapi` generates static MDX pages directly from our `openapi.json`\n(the same document `shalgalt-core` already serves at `/openapi.json`), so P7-03 is a\nfirst-class part of the site rather than a bolted-on redoc iframe."},"964":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#options-considered","content":"One theme, one search index (FlexSearch static client — works under `output: export`),\none deploy step."},"965":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#options-considered","content":"Two audience trees (`docs/dev`, `docs/user`) modelled as separate sidebar roots, with a\nsite-wide i18n locale switcher layered on top (see below)."},"966":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#decision","content":"The Next.js docs app lives in &#x2A;*`docs/site/`** as an isolated package (its own\n`package.json`, not part of the root SvelteKit install) so its Next.js dependency tree\nnever mixes with the app's SvelteKit/Tauri tree."},"967":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#decision","content":"MDX content lives in &#x2A;*`docs/dev/`*&#x2A; (English) and &#x2A;*`docs/user/`** (Mongolian), honouring\nthe directory layout master plan §12 prescribes. `docs/site/` only holds the framework."},"968":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#decision","content":"The build is fully static: `next.config` sets `output: \"export\"`, `trailingSlash: true`,\n`images.unoptimized: true`, and `basePath: \"/shalgalt-omr\"` (the GitHub Pages project\nsubpath). Search runs through `flexsearchStaticClient` + a `staticGET` route so it works\nwithout a server."},"969":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#decision","content":"The HTTP API reference (P7-03) is produced by running\n`cargo run -p shalgalt-core --example dump_openapi -- docs/site/openapi.json` and then\n`fumadocs-openapi`'s `generateFiles` into `docs/dev/api/`. The spec therefore cannot\ndrift from the router."},"970":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#internationalization-i18n","content":"The site is multilingual via Fumadocs i18n with two locales:"},"971":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#internationalization-i18n","content":"**`mn` (Mongolian) — the default locale.** The bare URL\n(`https://filename24.github.io/shalgalt-omr/`) serves Mongolian, matching the product's\nMongolian-only UI and the \"Mongolian-first\" priority."},"972":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#internationalization-i18n","content":"**`en` (English) — the secondary locale**, reachable via the locale switcher\n(`/shalgalt-omr/en/...`)."},"973":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#internationalization-i18n","content":"Content authoring follows the Fumadocs convention that an &#x2A;*unsuffixed file is the default\nlanguage (`mn`)** and a `*.en.mdx` file is the English version; a missing locale falls back\nto the default-language file. Two consequences flow from the repository's own language rules:"},"974":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#internationalization-i18n","content":"**Developer docs (`docs/dev/`) are authored in English** as unsuffixed `.mdx` files. The\nrepository rule \"code & documentation are English only\" forbids a Mongolian translation of\ndeveloper docs, so these pages render in English under **both** locales (the `en` locale\nresolves them directly; the `mn` locale shows the same English content). \"English-first when\ndeveloping\" is therefore satisfied automatically."},"975":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#internationalization-i18n","content":"**User-manual docs (`docs/user/`) are authored in Mongolian** as unsuffixed `.mdx`\n(the `mn` default) with `*.en.mdx` English translations added progressively. Untranslated\nuser pages fall back to Mongolian."},"976":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#internationalization-i18n","content":"Search is locale-aware (`createI18nSearchAPI` on the server side + `flexsearchStaticClient`\nwith the active locale on the client), and still runs fully in-browser under `output:\nexport`."},"977":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#github-pages-coexistence-with-the-updater-manifest","content":"`gh-pages` already hosts the `tauri-plugin-updater` manifest at\n`https://filename24.github.io/shalgalt-omr/latest.json` (ADR 0018, published by\n`release.yml`). The P6 publish step already uses `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v4` with\n`keep_files: true` precisely so documentation can land alongside it."},"978":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#github-pages-coexistence-with-the-updater-manifest","content":"The docs deploy workflow (`.github/workflows/docs.yml`) mirrors this: it publishes the\nstatic `out/` directory to the **root** of `gh-pages` with `keep_files: true`. Result:"},"979":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#github-pages-coexistence-with-the-updater-manifest","content":"`https://filename24.github.io/shalgalt-omr/` → documentation home."},"980":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#github-pages-coexistence-with-the-updater-manifest","content":"`https://filename24.github.io/shalgalt-omr/latest.json` → updater manifest (untouched)."},"981":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#github-pages-coexistence-with-the-updater-manifest","content":"Because both workflows use `keep_files: true`, neither clobbers the other's output."},"982":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#consequences","content":"**Positive**: one toolchain, one theme, one search, one deploy; first-class OpenAPI;\nAPI spec stays in sync with the router; docs and updater coexist on one branch."},"983":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#consequences","content":"**Negative**: introduces a Next.js/React dependency tree for docs only. Mitigated by\nisolating it in `docs/site/` (separate install) so it never touches the app build."},"984":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr/0019-docs-fumadocs-and-gh-pages#consequences","content":"**Follow-up**: per-release PDF exports of both manuals (master plan §12) are deferred to\na later docs iteration; the static HTML site is the v1.0 deliverable."},"985":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","type":"page","content":"Architecture Decisions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Architecture Decisions"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr"},"986":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr","content":"The significant, hard-to-reverse choices behind shalgalt-omr — what we picked, the alternatives, and the consequences accepted."},"987":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr#foundation--build","content":"Foundation & build"},"988":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr#pdf-generation--templates","content":"PDF generation & templates"},"989":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr#ui--theming","content":"UI & theming"},"990":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr#computer-vision-pipeline","content":"Computer-vision pipeline"},"991":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr#project-file-format","content":"Project file format"},"992":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr#http-api","content":"HTTP API"},"993":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/adr#distribution--documentation","content":"Distribution & documentation"},"994":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr","content":"Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) capture the choices that shaped shalgalt-omr: the\ncontext, the options weighed, the decision, and the consequences we accepted. They exist so\na future contributor can understand *why* the system looks the way it does without\nre-litigating settled questions."},"995":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr","content":"Write an ADR when a decision is **hard to reverse** (build toolchain, file format, IPC\ncontract), when **multiple credible options** exist with non-obvious trade-offs, or when a\nfuture contributor would otherwise ask the same question again. Small, local, easily\nreversible changes do not need one — just write the code."},"996":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr","content":"Every ADR below is **Accepted**. Re-opening a locked decision requires a *new* ADR plus a\nmaster-plan update in the same PR — see the master plan\nand the contribution guide."},"997":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#foundation--build","content":"How OpenCV is provisioned at build time across Windows, macOS, and Linux."},"998":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#foundation--build","content":"The monorepo split into `apps/*` hosts and pure `crates/*` libraries."},"999":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#foundation--build","content":"Generating the frontend's domain types from Rust so they never drift."},"1000":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#pdf-generation--templates","content":"Choosing a pure-Rust PDF engine with embedded Noto fonts over native bindings."},"1001":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#pdf-generation--templates","content":"Path-string commands and on-disk results — never bytes across the IPC boundary."},"1002":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#pdf-generation--templates","content":"A drawing-surface abstraction with per-element layout modules in `shalgalt-pdf`."},"1003":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#pdf-generation--templates","content":"Why option labels are printed inside the bubble circle."},"1004":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#ui--theming","content":"Light-by-default theming plus an opt-in comfortable type scale."},"1005":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#computer-vision-pipeline","content":"`DICT_6X6_50` markers (IDs 0–3, TL/TR/BR/BL) replace anonymous corner squares."},"1006":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#computer-vision-pipeline","content":"Per-bubble fill scoring, decision bands, and the `needs_review` rule."},"1007":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#computer-vision-pipeline","content":"Recovering perspective when fewer than four markers are detected."},"1008":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#project-file-format","content":"A zip container with an always-plaintext manifest."},"1009":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#project-file-format","content":"Passphrase-based, ASCII-armored `age` encryption for project payloads."},"1010":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#http-api","content":"Versioned routes, a storage seam in core, and OpenAPI via `utoipa`."},"1011":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#http-api","content":"A shared `rusqlite` `DataStore`, splitting the read path from plugin-sql writes."},"1012":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#http-api","content":"The uncommon default port (22345), desktop auto-fallback, and env override."},"1013":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#distribution--documentation","content":"Shipping signed bundles through GitHub Releases with `tauri-action`."},"1014":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#distribution--documentation","content":"`tauri-plugin-updater` with a static `gh-pages` manifest, default off."},"1015":{"id":"/mn/docs/adr-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/adr#distribution--documentation","content":"This Fumadocs site, deployed to GitHub Pages."},"1016":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"page","content":"Architecture decisions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr"},"1017":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","content":"How shalgalt-omr records architectural decisions — what an ADR is, when to write one, and the template to follow."},"1018":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#when-to-write-one","content":"When to write one"},"1019":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#file-naming","content":"File naming"},"1020":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#template-sections","content":"Template sections"},"1021":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#status--metadata","content":"Status & metadata"},"1022":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#context","content":"Context"},"1023":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#options","content":"Options"},"1024":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#decision","content":"Decision"},"1025":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"1026":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#follow-up","content":"Follow-up"},"1027":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#re-litigating-a-locked-decision","content":"Re-litigating a locked decision"},"1028":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","content":"An &#x2A;*Architecture Decision Record (ADR)** is a short document that captures a significant\narchitectural or operational choice: the context, the alternatives considered, the decision,\nand the consequences accepted. The value is in the *recorded reasoning* — so a future\ncontributor understands why the system looks the way it does without re-litigating settled\nquestions."},"1029":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","content":"The full set of accepted ADRs."},"1030":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#when-to-write-one","content":"The decision is **hard to reverse** — e.g. choice of build toolchain, database engine, or\nIPC contract."},"1031":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#when-to-write-one","content":"**Multiple credible options** exist and the trade-offs are non-obvious."},"1032":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#when-to-write-one","content":"A future contributor would otherwise **re-litigate the same question**."},"1033":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#when-to-write-one","content":"If a change is small, local, and easily reversible, it does not need an ADR — just write\nthe code."},"1034":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#file-naming","content":"ADRs live under `docs/adr/`, one file per decision:"},"1035":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#file-naming","content":"`NNNN` is a monotonically increasing four-digit number with **no gaps** — four digits keeps\nthe sort order stable past 100 entries."},"1036":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#template-sections","content":"Use the structure of an existing ADR. Keep it short — the value is in the recorded\nreasoning, not the prose volume."},"1037":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#status--metadata","content":"`Status` (Accepted / Superseded / …), `Date`, and `Deciders`."},"1038":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#context","content":"The forces and constraints that made this a real decision."},"1039":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#options","content":"The credible alternatives, with their trade-offs."},"1040":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#decision","content":"What was chosen, and the rationale."},"1041":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#consequences","content":"What this commits the project to — including the costs accepted."},"1042":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#follow-up","content":"Any deferred validation or related work the decision implies."},"1043":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/adr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/adr#re-litigating-a-locked-decision","content":"Every accepted ADR is **locked**. Re-opening one requires a *new* ADR **plus** a\nmaster-plan update in the same PR. Don't quietly contradict an accepted decision in code —\nrecord the change. See the contribution guide."},"1044":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","type":"page","content":"Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture"},"1045":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","content":"Layers, data flow, and the four hard rules that every PR must respect."},"1046":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Stack"},"1047":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#high-level-flow","content":"High-level flow"},"1048":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#the-four-hard-rules","content":"The four hard rules"},"1049":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#database-ownership","content":"Database ownership"},"1050":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#see-also","content":"See also"},"1051":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Layer"},"1052":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Technology"},"1053":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Frontend"},"1054":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"SvelteKit 5 (adapter-static, SSG), Svelte 5 runes, TailwindCSS v4"},"1055":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"UI kit"},"1056":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"shadcn-svelte (bits-ui + tailwind-variants), `@lucide/svelte` icons"},"1057":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Editor / UI"},"1058":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"svelte-konva (Canvas), paneforge (IDE panes)"},"1059":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Native shell"},"1060":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Tauri 2.0 + plugins: sql, dialog, fs, opener, log, single-instance, window-state, updater"},"1061":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Core"},"1062":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Rust — opencv-rust, pdfium-render, rust\\_xlsxwriter, printpdf"},"1063":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Persistence"},"1064":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"`tauri-plugin-sql` + SQLite (a single file in Tauri's `app_data_dir`)"},"1065":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Background API"},"1066":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"axum on `127.0.0.1:22345` (default; auto-fallback if busy)"},"1067":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"Async"},"1068":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#stack","content":"tokio (`full`)"},"1069":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#high-level-flow","content":"The desktop host (`apps/desktop`) is the only place that knows about Tauri. The four\n`crates/` are pure Rust and are reused by the standalone server (`apps/server`)."},"1070":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#the-four-hard-rules","content":"Every PR must respect these. They are the load-bearing invariants of the system — a change\nthat violates any of them is rejected in review."},"1071":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#the-four-hard-rules","content":"Tauri commands take `pdf_path: String` / `image_path: String`, never image or PDF\nbuffers. Result images are written to disk and the frontend loads them through the\n`asset://localhost/` protocol. This avoids the \"memory mirage\" where multi-hundred-MB\nscans would be serialized across the IPC boundary. The `.shalgalt` reader/writer\n(`shalgalt-fileformat`) streams entries for the same reason — a project never lands in a\nsingle `Vec<u8>`."},"1072":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#the-four-hard-rules","content":"Long-running work (grading a stack of sheets) runs in a `tokio::spawn`ed task. Progress\nis reported by emitting `task-progress` events with snake\\_case stage names\n(`TaskProgress` / `TaskStage` in `shalgalt-core::domain::progress`). The command thread\nreturns immediately."},"1073":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#the-four-hard-rules","content":"`OmrTemplate` (markers + bubble groups + answer key) serializes as **a single JSON\ndocument** into one `TEXT` column (`templates.json_schema`). It is never split into\nmultiple columns or denormalized. Coordinates are &#x2A;*normalized to `[0, 1]`** so a\ntemplate works across DPIs and page sizes. The Rust struct\n(`shalgalt-core::domain::template`) and the TypeScript interface (`src/lib/types/`) are\nkept in sync by `ts-rs` codegen — never hand-edit the generated TS."},"1074":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#the-four-hard-rules","content":"The `Router` and CORS layer are built in `shalgalt-core::api`. That crate never calls\n`axum::serve`, never binds a port, and never reads environment variables. The host owns\nthe lifecycle: `apps/desktop` wraps the router in a `tokio::spawn` + oneshot\ngraceful-shutdown harness; `apps/server` runs it as the process's main task. Routes are\nversioned under `/v1/`; breaking changes require a version bump and an ADR."},"1075":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#database-ownership","content":"All database access goes through `tauri-plugin-sql`. There is **no `sqlx` pool on the Rust\nside**. Migrations are defined in Rust (`apps/desktop/src/lib.rs`, SQL embedded via\n`include_str!`). The frontend reads and writes through `src/lib/db/*`. Rust commands never\ntouch the database: when a Rust task produces data that must be persisted (e.g. grading\nresults), it emits an event and the frontend writes it."},"1076":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#database-ownership","content":"The standalone server uses a separate read-mostly `rusqlite` `DataStore` in\n`shalgalt-store` — see ADR 0014."},"1077":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#see-also","content":"What each crate and app owns."},"1078":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#see-also","content":"The `/v1/` surface."},"1079":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/architecture#see-also","content":"The per-crate `AGENTS.md` files are authoritative for module-shape decisions; the ADRs\nrecord why the system looks the way it does."},"1080":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"page","content":"Build & run","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build"},"1081":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build","content":"System prerequisites and build/run commands for each OS."},"1082":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#system-prerequisites","content":"System prerequisites"},"1083":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#pdfium-runtime-all-platforms","content":"pdfium (runtime, all platforms)"},"1084":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#toolchains","content":"Toolchains"},"1085":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Common commands"},"1086":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#first-run","content":"First run"},"1087":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#running-the-standalone-http-server","content":"Running the standalone HTTP server"},"1088":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build","content":"shalgalt-omr depends on native libraries (OpenCV for the CV pipeline, pdfium at runtime,\nplus the platform webview toolkit for Tauri). Install the system prerequisites first, then\nthe JS and Rust toolchains."},"1089":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#system-prerequisites","content":"Per ADR 0001 the project uses the upstream OpenCV\nprebuilt self-extractor. LLVM (for opencv-rust's bindgen) ships with recent Visual Studio\ninstalls; otherwise install it from llvm.org."},"1090":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#system-prerequisites","content":"Bumping OpenCV means updating three places: the snippet above, the `OPENCV_VERSION`\njob-level env in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, and\nADR 0001."},"1091":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#pdfium-runtime-all-platforms","content":"`pdfium-render` looks up the pdfium dynamic library at runtime. Download a release for your\nOS from bblanchon/pdfium-binaries and place\nit next to the executable, or extend `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` (Linux) / `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` (macOS)\n/ `PATH` (Windows). Release bundles ship pdfium as a bundled resource."},"1092":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#toolchains","content":"**Node** ≥ 20 and **pnpm** (the repo pins versions via `package.json` / `pnpm-lock.yaml`)."},"1093":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#toolchains","content":"**Rust** stable (`rustup`), with `cargo fmt` and `clippy` components."},"1094":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Command"},"1095":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Purpose"},"1096":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm install`"},"1097":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Install JS dependencies."},"1098":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm dev`"},"1099":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"SvelteKit dev server only (browser, no Tauri webview)."},"1100":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm tauri dev`"},"1101":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Native window + Rust core (auto-runs Vite). The default flow."},"1102":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm check`"},"1103":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`svelte-kit sync` + `svelte-check`."},"1104":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm build`"},"1105":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Build SvelteKit assets (consumed by `tauri build`)."},"1106":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm tauri build`"},"1107":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Production native bundle."},"1108":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"`pnpm generate-types`"},"1109":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Regenerate TS bindings from Rust (`cargo test -p shalgalt-core`)."},"1110":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#common-commands","content":"Run these at the workspace root for the Rust side:"},"1111":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#first-run","content":"On first launch the SQL plugin creates the SQLite file in the OS-specific data directory\n(e.g. Linux `~/.local/share/dev.filename.shalgalt-omr/`, macOS\n`~/Library/Application Support/dev.filename.shalgalt-omr/`) and applies migrations\nautomatically."},"1112":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/build-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/build#running-the-standalone-http-server","content":"See the HTTP API reference for CLI flags, bind address, and auth behaviour."},"1113":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"page","content":"Contributing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing"},"1114":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","content":"Branching model, commit conventions, language rules, and the PR checklist."},"1115":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"Branching model"},"1116":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#commit-conventions","content":"Commit conventions"},"1117":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"Language rules (mandatory)"},"1118":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#the-four-hard-rules","content":"The four hard rules"},"1119":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#adrs","content":"ADRs"},"1120":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"PR checklist"},"1121":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"Continuous integration"},"1122":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"**`stable`** — release branch. CI publishes from here. Never commit directly."},"1123":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"**`develop`** — integration branch. Feature PRs land here."},"1124":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"**`feat/<phase>-<topic>`** — work branches off `develop`. One feature per PR."},"1125":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#branching-model","content":"`session/*` branches are local isolation only and must never be pushed to the remote."},"1126":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#commit-conventions","content":"Conventional Commits, one short imperative subject line:"},"1127":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#commit-conventions","content":"Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `test`, `perf`, `ci`."},"1128":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"Two languages, no overlap:"},"1129":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"Every comment, doc comment, identifier, log message, error string, commit message, PR\ndescription, and Markdown file in the repo."},"1130":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"Page titles, buttons, labels, validation and toast messages, help text. UI strings come\nfrom the single string table at `src/lib/i18n/`; components never hard-code copy."},"1131":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#language-rules-mandatory","content":"`AppError.code` stays English (it is a stable identifier); the frontend maps the code to a\nMongolian message in the string table. A reviewer should treat any non-English string in\nsource or docs as a blocker, and any hard-coded user-facing string outside the i18n table\nas a blocker too."},"1132":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#the-four-hard-rules","content":"A change is rejected if it violates any of the four architecture rules:\npath-strings-only IPC, no UI freeze on batch work, single-JSON template format, and the\nhost-owned axum lifecycle. When in doubt, read the relevant crate's `AGENTS.md`."},"1133":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#adrs","content":"Architectural or operational decisions that are hard to reverse get an ADR under\n`docs/adr/` (`NNNN-kebab-title.md`, no gaps). Re-litigating a locked decision requires a new\nADR **plus** a master-plan update in the same PR. See how we write ADRs and the\nfull Architecture Decisions collection."},"1134":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"Before requesting review:"},"1135":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"`cargo fmt --all -- --check` is clean."},"1136":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` is clean."},"1137":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"`cargo test --workspace` passes (unit + integration + ts-rs export)."},"1138":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"`pnpm check` passes (no Rust↔TS type drift)."},"1139":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"New behaviour has tests; coverage target is 80%+."},"1140":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"No non-English strings in code/docs; no hard-coded UI copy outside the i18n table."},"1141":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"No secrets committed; the axum server still binds `127.0.0.1` by default."},"1142":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-28","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#pr-checklist","content":"Branch is rebased on `develop` and conflicts are resolved."},"1143":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-29","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"CI runs on every push to `develop`/`stable` and on PRs targeting them:"},"1144":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-30","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"Job"},"1145":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-31","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"Purpose"},"1146":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-32","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"`web-check`"},"1147":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-33","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `svelte-kit sync`, `pnpm check`."},"1148":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-34","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"`rust-check`"},"1149":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-35","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"apt deps → `cargo fmt --check` → `clippy -D warnings` → `cargo check`."},"1150":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing-36","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/contributing#continuous-integration","content":"Both jobs must be green before merge. Release bundling (signed installers, pdfium download,\npackaging) and the updater manifest are handled by `release.yml` on `v*` tags. The\ndocumentation site is built and published to GitHub Pages by `docs.yml`."},"1151":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev"},"1152":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev","content":"Developer documentation for shalgalt-omr — a local-first OMR grading IDE."},"1153":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"1154":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#design","content":"Design"},"1155":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#generate","content":"Generate"},"1156":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#grade","content":"Grade"},"1157":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#review","content":"Review"},"1158":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#export","content":"Export"},"1159":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#core-principles","content":"Core principles"},"1160":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"Where to start"},"1161":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev","content":"shalgalt-omr is a **local-first OMR (Optical Mark Recognition) grading IDE**: a Tauri 2\ndesktop application with a SvelteKit frontend and a Rust core that grades scanned OMR PDFs\nfully offline, persists results in SQLite, and exposes an optional background HTTP API for\nintegrations."},"1162":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev","content":"This site has two audiences:"},"1163":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev","content":"Architecture, the Cargo workspace map, how to build and run on each OS, the contribution\nworkflow, the ADR index, and the HTTP API reference."},"1164":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev","content":"Installation and day-to-day use of the application."},"1165":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-13","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#design","content":"Lay out an OMR answer sheet in a visual editor (ArUco corner markers + bubble groups)."},"1166":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-14","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#generate","content":"Produce a printable PDF of that sheet."},"1167":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-15","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#grade","content":"Process stacks of scanned/photographed sheets offline using an OpenCV pipeline\n(adaptive threshold, auto-deskew, per-bubble confidence scoring)."},"1168":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-16","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#review","content":"Inspect low-confidence sheets bubble-by-bubble."},"1169":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-17","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#export","content":"Write results to Excel, or share a whole project as an encrypted `.shalgalt` file."},"1170":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-18","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#core-principles","content":"No telemetry, no crash reporting, no analytics. Nothing leaves the machine unless the\nuser explicitly exports it. The optional HTTP API binds to `127.0.0.1` by default."},"1171":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-19","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#core-principles","content":"All **code and documentation are English**; all **end-user UI text is Mongolian**\n(Cyrillic). See the language conventions in the repo `AGENTS.md`."},"1172":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-20","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#core-principles","content":"Four hard rules (IPC path-strings only, no UI freeze on batch work, a single-JSON\ntemplate format, an axum router that never owns its own lifecycle) are enforced on every\nPR."},"1173":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-21","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"New to the codebase? Start here, then read the workspace map."},"1174":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-22","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"What each crate and app owns."},"1175":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-23","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"Trying to build it? System prerequisites and commands per OS."},"1176":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-24","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"Branching, commit conventions, language rules, and the PR checklist."},"1177":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-25","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"How the Rust and frontend test suites are organized and run."},"1178":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-26","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"Integrating over HTTP? The `/v1/` surface."},"1179":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev-27","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev#where-to-start","content":"The authoritative sources remain the repository's `AGENTS.md` files (one per crate) and\nthe master plan at `.claude/PRPs/plans/shalgalt-omr-master.plan.md`. This site condenses\nthem; where they disagree, the code wins for behaviour and the per-package `AGENTS.md`\nwins for module-shape decisions."},"1180":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"page","content":"Testing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing"},"1181":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","content":"How the Rust and frontend test suites are organized and run."},"1182":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"Rust"},"1183":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-2","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#frontend","content":"Frontend"},"1184":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-3","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#generated-artifacts-used-by-docs","content":"Generated artifacts used by docs"},"1185":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-4","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#coverage-target","content":"Coverage target"},"1186":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-5","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"Unit tests live in `#[cfg(test)]` modules next to the code; integration tests live in each\ncrate's `tests/` directory (one binary per file). Run everything from the workspace root:"},"1187":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-6","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"Notable suites:"},"1188":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-7","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"`template_serde` round-trips an `OmrTemplate` against a golden fixture\n(`tests/fixtures/template-v1.json`), catching accidental Rule 3 schema breakage. The\ngrading engine has unit coverage for scoring, partial answer keys, and confidence\nbanding. The `/v1/` router is exercised in-process over a `MemoryStore` without binding a\nsocket."},"1189":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-8","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"`roundtrip` (write → read, encrypted and plaintext, streamed 1 MiB entry, deterministic\norder, manifest-has-no-PII), `bad_passphrase`, and `forward_compat` (a `format_version`\nnewer than supported is refused before any decryption)."},"1190":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-9","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#rust","content":"Fixture-driven detection tests under `tests/fixtures/`."},"1191":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-10","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#frontend","content":"Unit tests cover utilities, data transforms, and stores. Type generation drift (Rust struct\nvs generated TS) surfaces as a `pnpm check` failure."},"1192":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-11","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#generated-artifacts-used-by-docs","content":"Two examples produce artifacts the documentation consumes — they are also a lightweight\nsmoke test that the public APIs still compile:"},"1193":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing-12","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/testing#coverage-target","content":"The repo targets &#x2A;*80%+** coverage on business logic. Prefer fixing the implementation over\nweakening a test; only change a test when the test itself is wrong."},"1194":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","type":"page","content":"Workspace map","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace"},"1195":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-0","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","content":"The Cargo workspace — what each app and crate owns."},"1196":{"id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace-1","page_id":"/mn/docs/dev/workspace","ty