behind a\nuser setting."],[1459,"3 минутын танилцуулга видеоны дүр зураг."],[21,"30–60 min"],[23,"30–60 min"],[375,"4"],[808,"4"],[812,"4"],[810,"4 correspondences, exact fit"],[1411,"4 булангийн **ArUco тэмдэг** бүгд зурагт бүтэн орсон эсэхийг шалга."],[1481,"5 минутын танилцуулга видеоны дүр зураг."],[436,"6 pt glyph hull (rough): ≈ 1.0 mm²"],[24,"6–15 MB"],[369,"8"],[749,"8080 is one of the most contended ports on a developer or teacher machine — Tomcat,\nJenkins, countless dev servers, and corporate proxies all default to it. Worse, the desktop\nbinder had two failure problems when 8080 was taken:"],[613,"A `.shalgalt` project bundles student-identifying data: a roster (`students.csv`) and graded\nresults tied to names. When a teacher emails a project, drops it on a shared drive, or carries\nit on a USB stick, that PII is exposed. We want **optional** at-rest encryption so a teacher can\nprotect a project with a passphrase, while keeping unencrypted projects trivially inspectable\nfor the common case."],[737,"A bundled Release asset for `shalgalt-server` lands in P6 (`release.yml`)."],[331,"A Canvas drawing-surface wrapper plus a module-per-visual-element layout split for shalgalt-pdf."],[1132,"A change is rejected if it violates any of the four architecture rules:\npath-strings-only IPC, no UI freeze on batch work, single-JSON template format, and the\nhost-owned axum lifecycle. When in doubt, read the relevant crate's `AGENTS.md`."],[760,"A common alt (8000/8888/9000)"],[1002,"A drawing-surface abstraction with per-element layout modules in `shalgalt-pdf`."],[695,"A future `/v2/` (if ever needed) keeps `/v1/` alive for one release for integrators."],[605,"A future `format_version: 2` (if the layout ever changes) must ship with a migration note and\na loader that still reads version 1."],[237,"A future `prebuild` hook on `apps/web` could run the codegen automatically before\n`pnpm dev` starts; not pressing while the test-driven check covers CI."],[1032,"A future contributor would otherwise **re-litigate the same question**."],[398,"A future LayoutMap sidecar (AMC's `.xy` pattern, master-plan D4) will plug into the\nCanvas at the call site without changing the wrapper API."],[349,"A market survey of mainstream OMR tools (AMC, Remark Office, OMRChecker, OpenMCR,\nZipGrade) confirmed that **none** drives `printpdf`-equivalent low-level ops directly:\nAMC sits on `pdfTeX`, Remark on Word, the others ship pre-baked PDFs. The closest\nprior art for our pure-Rust path is AMC's `automultiplechoice.sty` LaTeX wrapper, which\nis *itself* a thin DSL over a lower-level engine."],[831,"A new integration test (`three_markers_still_align`) drops the TL marker and asserts a\nknown filled bubble still reads `> 0.65`, which also locks in the corner-ordering\ncorrespondence. `deliberately_bad` now blacks out two top markers so the\n\"fails gracefully\" assertion stays deterministic under the ≥3 rule."],[598,"A new pure-Rust crate `crates/shalgalt-fileformat` owns read/write. It depends on `zip`\n(no default features — the bzip2/zstd/xz/aes C codecs are dropped) and, for the encrypted\ncase, `age`. It deliberately does **not** depend on `shalgalt-core`: it streams opaque named\nbyte blobs and stays domain-agnostic, so the `OmrTemplate`/`AnswerKey` types remain solely\nin `shalgalt-core::domain`."],[718,"A read-only rusqlite connection"],[716,"A read-write rusqlite connection"],[762,"A registered-range, uncommon port"],[713,"A shared `crates/shalgalt-store`"],[1011,"A shared `rusqlite` `DataStore`, splitting the read path from plugin-sql writes."],[697,"A shared rusqlite DataStore implementation, with the desktop's read path split from plugin-sql writes."],[883,"A single `v*` tag produces a complete, downloadable Release: Windows installer +\n`shalgalt-server`, with macOS/Linux ready to enable."],[787,"A teacher whose machine already runs something on 22345 gets a working app on 22346+,\nwith the real port discoverable from `api-endpoint.json